      "title": "Program Manager, Upward Bound - Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement (Madison County)",
      "description": "Program Manager, Upward Bound - Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement (Madison County) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63497 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Center for Academic Retention & Enhancement Responsibilities In conjunction with departmental leadership, ensures that the Upward Bound Madison County program is implemented in full compliance with department, university, and grant sponsor policies, and all other applicable federal regulations and requirements. Manages implementation of the program’s activities, goals and objectives, guided by the funded proposal, federal/ state regulations, and University polices and priorities while keeping the program objectives in mind. Executes the plan of operation by informing the community about program, identifying and selecting participants, assessing students, developing individual action plans, assigning services, monitoring participants' progress, and retaining and graduating students. Directly supervises and develops program staff. In accordance with all applicable federal, state and university regulations, effectively manages program budgets in concert with departmental leadership and divisional finance/ human resources staff. Manages services for program participants including, but not limited to tutoring, high school graduation advisement, financial aid & literacy, college enrollment, academic counseling, career exploration, mentoring, personal counseling services, and enrichment activities. Provides and facilitates individual and group services to students such as advising, mentoring, tutoring, workshops, and supplemental instruction. Monitors and maintains appropriate documentation and records, including student participant records, in accordance with federal and university regulations in conjunction with departmental leadership. Coordinates the development and maintenance of all program forms, including participant applications, evaluation forms, program brochures, and similar publications. Promote positive working relationships with campus partners; Serve on department, division or university committees; Participate in professional development; Perform other similarly-related duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience related to academic and/or student services; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience related to academic and/or student services. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree. Adhere to ethical business practices and promote ethical behavior. Communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Demonstrate critical thinking based upon in-depth data, substantiating information, considering and respecting others' input personal values, and ethics. Knowledge of and the ability to interpret and apply related University policies, procedures, principles, and practices. Knowledge of the principles and practices of event planning and ability to coordinate, organize and evaluate meetings and/or events. Knowledge of the principles and practices of project planning, development, and evaluation. Knowledge of the concepts, principles, and practices of accounting, budgeting, and cost control procedures. Contact Info Stacy Spencer University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Low to high $50,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position requires traveling to Madison County. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63811&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Senior Student Athlete Academic Coordinator, Level I",
      "description": "Senior Student Athlete Academic Coordinator, Level I Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63811 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Student Athlete Academic Services (SAAS) Responsibilities Serves as an academic advisor for assigned student-athletes in Football and olympic sports. More specifically, duties include but are not limited to monitoring NCAA academic eligibility, academic advising, providing individualized academic support services, coordinating study table, and attending weekly coaches/oversight meetings to provide information related to student-athlete academic progress. Will also be responsible for providing academic progress updates to the Assistant Dean/Associate Athletics Director of SAAS, Football coaching staff members, and athletics administration. May assist with or one or more administrative programs in SAAS. Responsible for keeping the Assistant Dean/Associate Athletics Director of SAAS, Dean of Undergraduate Studies, and appropriate athletics department staff informed about current and future needs to support SAAS and provide comprehensive academic advising and support programs for student-athletes. Involved in the recruitment of prospective student-athletes which includes interaction with recruits and their families, coaches, faculty and staff members, and alumni. Serve as liaison between Undergraduate Studies, Athletic Department, faculty, Admissions, Registrar, Financial Aid, and other Academic Departments. Has occasional contact with the media and officials from the ACC and NCAA. Other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and four years of experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Preferred Qualifications Master's Degree. Knowledge of NCAA rules and regulations. Experience working with student-athletes by monitoring their academic progress and employment of educational strategies. Experience in presenting educational workshops for student-athletes. Experience with academic advising/oversight in a secondary or post-secondary setting. Experience working independently and prioritizing work under deadlines. Experience working with individuals from various academic and economic backgrounds. Ability to supervise staff. Ability to interpret and explain policies to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Attention to detail and the highest standard of integrity are imperative. Ability to deal with people calmly, confidently and with complete objectivity. Experience with Microsoft Office programs. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63798&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Admissions Associates (Part-Time/OPS)",
      "description": "Admissions Associates (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63798 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Admissions Associates play a vital role in creating a welcoming and positive experience for our guests. Typical responsibilities include: Providing exceptional customer service to guests Answering questions, providing information, and selling: Tickets Tours Memberships Processing payments and ticket distribution As needed: Assist with admissions for events Provides additional support as assigned Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Preferred Qualifications Ability to: Handle cash and various forms of payment(s) Remain positive and calm during peak times and higher customer volume Work independently and with a team Effective communication skills (in person, via telephone, and email) Verbal fluency in additional language(s) besides English Previous Tessitura experience or the ability to learn/use a web-based computer ticketing system Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.45 per hour How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Work Location: Sarasota, FL. Based on the duties, this position will require completion of a criminal history background check. Employees are required to adhere to business dress standards. Working Hours Up to 24 hours a week with an arrival time of 8:45 AM. Please note that weekends, evenings, and holidays are required based on the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63816&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Media Coordinator/Librarian - The Florida Channel",
      "description": "Assistant Media Coordinator/Librarian - The Florida Channel Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63816 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Florida Channel Responsibilities Ensures all legislative sessions and designated meetings, programs, segments and events are ingested, routed to modulator channels and webcasts, monitored for audio/video quality, and entered into databases. Operates all equipment necessary to perform tasks, including but not limited to media capture tools, media and traffic databases, editor, monitors, router and intercom system. Troubleshoots and communicates issues with clarity. Catalogues, organizes, and maintains physical and digital content libraries. Reviews and digitizes physical media and adds searchable metadata. Assists in processing dub requests. Monitors archive space regularly and archives files as needed. Checks video assets for file name consistency. In the absence of the Media Coordinator/Librarian, creates monthly productivity reports, updates the department manual and assists with other administrative tasks. Assists in other departments, including Web and Master Control. Serves as crew member for a variety of The Florida Channel programming. Qualifications Associate’s degree in a related area and 3 years of appropriate experience or vocational/technical training with 3 years of appropriate experience. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The schedule includes hours that may vary depending on department needs and may include weekends and evenings. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63815&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Acting and Movement, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre",
      "description": "Assistant Professor of Acting and Movement, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63815 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Theatre Responsibilities The Florida State University School of Theatre invites applications for a nine-month, tenure-track Assistant Professor of Acting and Movement position with a 3/3 teaching load to begin in August, 2027. We are seeking an artist, teacher, and collaborator with a dynamic and adaptable skillset to teach a variety of performance courses. Candidates should demonstrate a strong methodology for contemporary actor training. We seek a candidate who values and prioritizes empathy, integrity, and rigor in the development of the actor. Responsibilities include teaching undergraduate performance and movement courses across the BFA Acting, BFA Music Theatre, and BA Theatre programs. The position also requires serving on School and University committees, assisting with student recruitment and mentoring, participating in productions and/or other School of Theatre activities as appropriate, and working collaboratively with faculty and staff to fulfill the professional training and educational mission of the School of Theatre. Qualifications MFA in Acting or equivalent terminal degree. Evidence of sustained professional practice and/or research in theatre, film, television or equivalent media. Demonstrated record of achievement in teaching, academic research, and service. Academic teaching and directing experience are expected. Preferred Qualifications Interest in directing in the School of Theatre’s production season. Active union memberships in AEA and/or SAG-AFTRA. Contact Info Questions may be directed to Search Committee Chair, Matthew Schmidli , Teaching Faculty University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates should submit the following materials: Cover letter Current CV Statement of teaching philosophy An artist statement speaking to their creative scholarship Three recent letters of recommendation Please submit all application materials through the university’s online application system. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Applicant Review will begin November 30, 2026, and continue until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63818&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Control Technician 1",
      "description": "Control Technician 1 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63818 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities Maintenance Responsibilities Perform advanced troubleshooting tasks for complex building systems such as variable speed drive replacement, machine specific controllers repair or replacement, air compressors controls, boiler controls, heat exchangers, fume hoods, lab controls, and chiller controls. Perform network diagnostics for FLN and BLN Ethernet and other communication systems. Must be able to set up TECs on BACNet, P1, ModBus, KNX and other networks used in the control systems. Perform all tasks as described in the Maintenance Technician position description including basic mechanical, electrical, control, and plumbing tasks. Perform calibrations for sensors, controllers, flow meters, and other measurement devices. Coordinate with the Siemens onsite support technician to identify and repair components causing system faults. Coordinate with the energy engineer and other FSU team members to resolve complex system problems. Qualifications High school diploma and two years' experience or a post high school education and experience equal to two years. A relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
