      "title": "Administrative Associate (Statistics)",
      "description": "Administrative Associate (Statistics) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63793 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Statistics | Florida State University College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Administrative Associate is the first point of contact for all students, faculty, and guests of the Department of Statistics main office. In this role you will be responsible for: Serving as the point of contact for the Department of Statistics by answering the telephone, greeting walk-in visitors, and answering general questions via phone, email, and in-person. Processing and distributing outgoing and incoming mail. Assisting with assigning student offices and ordering keys. Serving as the departmental travel representative by assisting with travel arrangements, processing travel requests and reimbursements, and scheduling itineraries for visitors when needed. Serving as the departmental procurement representative by placing, monitoring, and receiving orders, preparing payment requests, and reconciling procurement card purchases. Serving as the Departmental Time & Leave Coordinator. Assisting with entering HR transactions for departmental personnel. Assisting the Chair and Business Manager with various tasks. Assisting with Promotion and Tenure tasks. Preparing announcements and assisting with scheduling and organizing events in departmental spaces. Ordering and maintaining departmental supply inventory. Performing on-campus errands. Assisting with reporting maintenance issues. Assisting with the use of office equipment. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and three years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience working in an office environment. Exceptional customer service skills. Excellent multitasking and organizational skills. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated starting salary for the position is in the mid $30,000's. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63473&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Admissions & Workflows Analyst",
      "description": "Admissions & Workflows Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63473 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Division of Enrollment Management - Technology Operations Unit Responsibilities The Division of Enrollment Management is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar , Office of Financial Aid , and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management’s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the students’ development and progression in their academic experience – from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families as well as to campus partners across the University. The Technology Operations Unit within Enrollment Management provides technology support, technology-based solutions, systems configuration, identity and data management, and analysis across the division. The unit works closely with subject matter experts in Admissions, Registrar, and Financial Aid to meet the operational and reporting needs of various stockholders across campus. Works collaboratively with Admissions staff and campus stakeholders to develop scalable solutions that improve data integrity, application processing, communication delivery, and student experience. Develops and maintains Slate workflows, forms, queries, rules, communications, and related system functionality. Analyzes business processes and operational requirements to identify opportunities for automation, efficiency, and process improvement through Slate. Develops and maintains advanced reporting tools to guide decision-making and improve recruitment effectiveness. Stays current on Slate capabilities and best practices and actively engages with peer institutions to share ideas and improve processes. Evaluates new feature requests and assesses their potential impact and feasibility. Serves as liaison and Slate support resource for designated talent-based admissions programs and populations, including but not limited to Music, Dance, Theatre, Studio Art, and Film. Collaborates with program staff and campus partners to develop and maintain application and review processes that support program objectives. Coordinates with departmental stakeholders to reconcile data, identify process issues, send communications to prospective students, and improve applicant experiences. Supports the day-to-day operations of the undergraduate Slate system by maintaining documentation, ensuring data integrity, and providing responsive support to internal and external users. Contributes to the Admissions knowledgebase and delivers training to new users to promote consistent and effective use of Slate. Participates in special events hosted by the Office of Admissions. Assists other sections during peak times in support of the goals of Enrollment Management. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications The ability to prioritize and organize multiple work assignments simultaneously. Experience with data management as well as using Microsoft Word, Excel, and Outlook or comparable software. Demonstrable technical experience to include handling configuration changes, modifications, enhancements and/or workarounds related to an application. Applicants should be able to establish and maintain effective working relationships and be able to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Preferred applicants should have a strong understanding of University admissions and recruitment processes. Previous work experience with admissions CRMs (Slate). Candidates with a strong sense of initiative and the demonstrated ability to manage multiple responsibilities concurrently are preferred. The ability to make sound judgments while working in a deadline-driven environment is essential. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $47,660, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63802&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director, Annual Giving Affinity & Colleges, Schools and Units Philanthropy & Engagement",
      "description": "Assistant Director, Annual Giving Affinity & Colleges, Schools and Units Philanthropy & Engagement Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63802 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional donor relations professionals’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Assistant Director provides strategic leadership and primary responsibility for the fundraising performance of an expansive portfolio of FSU affinity programs, colleges, schools, units, Alumni Association Networks, and faculty and staff philanthropy and engagement. Serving as the strategy lead for assigned areas, the position develops and directs comprehensive fundraising strategies designed to increase donors, philanthropic revenue, participation, and engagement. The Assistant Director provides strategic direction and recommendations to university partners and leads integrated, omni-channel solicitation strategies, including audience segmentation, messaging, planning, implementation, analysis, and optimization. The position collaborates across University Advancement and the university to establish fundraising priorities, goals, and processes, identify opportunities for growth, and ensure strategies are effectively executed and evaluated. Lead and manage comprehensive annual giving strategies and solicitation calendars for a portfolio of FSU-affiliated programs, colleges, schools, units, and affinity-based initiatives, with accountability for achieving established donor and revenue goals. Develop, execute, and optimize customized, integrated solicitation strategies for each assigned program based on fundraising priorities, donor audiences, performance data, and opportunities for growth. Direct omni-channel campaigns across direct mail, email, text messaging, digital advertising, social media, broadcast voicemail, and other emerging channels. Serve as the primary annual giving strategist and fundraising partner for assigned areas, establishing campaign priorities, recommending solicitation approaches, coordinating implementation, and ensuring fundraising plans align with broader University Advancement goals. Monitor and evaluate portfolio performance, using donor, revenue, response, and engagement data to identify opportunities, adjust strategies, and drive continued growth in philanthropic participation and giving. Support and enhance the stewardship activities of the programs. Analyze and evaluate the performance of omni-channel fundraising campaigns, using key donor, revenue, response, and engagement metrics to measure effectiveness, identify opportunities for growth, and inform future solicitation and annual giving strategies. Provide strategic fundraising guidance and recommendations to unit fundraisers and university leadership, using performance data, donor behavior, and annual giving best practices to develop strategies that strengthen donor retention, increase giving, and build sustainable philanthropic support. Build and manage relationships with donors, prospects, and external stakeholders through meetings and meaningful engagement, identifying opportunities to deepen philanthropic involvement and advance University and unit fundraising priorities. Ensure the integrity and accuracy of donor and fundraising data for assigned programs within the Division of University Advancement’s data management system, supporting effective solicitation, reporting, and strategic decision-making. Monitor and assess fundraising performance against established fiscal-year goals for each assigned college, school, unit, and program. Conduct bi-weekly progress reviews and develop quarterly performance recaps to identify trends, opportunities, and areas requiring strategic adjustment. Serve as the primary annual giving liaison and subject-matter expert for assigned programs, developing strong working knowledge of their priorities, donor audiences, and philanthropic opportunities while representing annual giving strategy within each area. Maintain appropriate confidentiality and stewardship of sensitive donor, prospect, and information in accordance with university and Division of University Advancement policies and practices. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) A valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63799&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (English)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (English) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63799 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of English | College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The Department of English at Florida State University seeks to appoint a tenure-track Assistant Professor to begin Fall 2027. We seek candidates who specialize in any area of pre-1700 non-dramatic English literature. We are open to a range of methodological approaches, and our aim is to identify exceptional scholarship. The appointee is expected to offer a range of courses in pre-1700 literature and to be a part of the rotation of teaching the department's Literary History 1 (pre-1800) survey required of Literature majors. Teaching assignment is two courses per semester, with one graduate course per year, plus supervision of graduate work at the MA and PhD levels. Qualifications A PhD from an accredited institution or the highest degree appropriate in a related field at the time of appointment is required. Contact Info Questions should be directed to Dr. Gary Taylor . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. A cover letter and CV should be included. After the initial review of applications, applicants selected for preliminary interviews will be asked to submit additional materials. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63784&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Spatial Data Science (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried - Spatial Data Science (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63784 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Social Sciences and Public Policy Responsibilities The successful candidates will have an academic home in one of the departments of the College which will be responsible for teaching assignments. Normally, the assignment is two courses per semester during the 9-month academic year. Contribute to research and scholarship through high quality publications in top-tier venues. Introductory undergraduate, advanced undergraduate, and graduate courses related to some aspect in the candidate's area of specialization. Standard service responsibilities with rank. Qualifications Ph.D. in any field related to spatial data science. Ability to demonstrate clear potential to produce frontier research in any aspect of spatial data science. An established record of successful teaching at the university level, commensurate with the rank being sought, and a demonstrated ability to teach and participate in the Department's undergraduate and graduate programs. Other Information The College of Social Sciences & Public Policy at Florida State University invites applications for two tenure-track appointments at the Assistant Professor level to begin August 2027. We seek individuals in any area of spatial data science who would work within the newly created Spatial Data Science Center (SDSC) under the Directorship of Professor A. Stewart Fotheringham. The Spatial Data Science Center (SDSC) brings together some of the world's most prominent experts in the field. It currently consists of 12 faculty members and 18 Ph.D students dedicated to advancing knowledge and practice in spatial data analytics. The Spatial Data Science Center (SDSC) is committed to developing solutions to some of society's most pressing problems in areas such as health, transportation, crime, poverty, and the environment through the power of spatial data analytics. To support this mission, the center also has dedicated space and resources designed to foster collaboration, innovation, and impact. The successful candidates will be dynamic and innovative, with demonstrated commitment to maintain an active research program that will yield high-quality research publications and external grand submissions. The candidates will also demonstrate and value high quality teaching and mentoring at both undergraduate and graduate levels. Contact Info Stewart Fotheringham University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Applicants must attach to the application: Cover Letter. Curriculum Vitae. Statement of research interests. Statement of teaching philosophy and experience. Copies of up to three relevant publications. Names and contact information for three professional references. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Review of applications begins December 1, 2026 and continues until the position is filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63801&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Director, Principal Gifts and Donor Experience",
      "description": "Associate Director, Principal Gifts and Donor Experience Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63801 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Division of University Advancement Florida State University is currently in the leadership phase of a comprehensive campaign. As the leadership phase of the campaign begins, the Division of University Advancement is accelerating the hiring of additional donor relations professionals’ campus-wide and is excited to build out its team. For Advancement professionals who are interested in being a part of a comprehensive campaign from the beginning for their career development, the timing is ideal to join our team. Responsibilities The Associate Director, Principal Gifts and Donor Experience is responsible for developing, maintaining and executing donor relations activities that complement our fundraisers’ external, face-to-face work for major and principal donors. Efforts will primarily focus on donors with $1 million+ lifetime giving. Working closely with the Donor Relations team, University Advancement leadership and other key leaders and staff across the university, this individual will be a strategic partner responsible for designing and implementing stewardship, recognition and engagement strategies, including high-touch donor experiences ranging from premium athletic hospitality to customized engagement opportunities. Additionally, they will create individualized communications to support this work and ensure donor engagement and satisfaction. Stewardship, Recognition and Engagement Create and implement new principal donor standards, practices and procedures aimed at stewarding, celebrating, thanking and engaging donors in unique and customized ways. Regularly collaborate with the Principal Gifts team and other leaders across Florida State University to develop and manage personalized donor relations plans for major and principal donors. This includes creating tailored impact reports and identifying and implementing distinctive and creative ways to recognize and engage these donors. Oversee complex stewardship and recognition projects that often include multiple deliverables. Develop efficient and effective systems to monitor and manage individual donor plans proactively. Assist with the collection of data, written reports and other materials as needed to steward gifts. Work with the donor relations team to oversee and assist with other key recognition programs. Identify ways to create tiered approaches for principal donors within existing and new programs and projects. Donor Communication Develop and deliver tailored communications for high-priority and principal donors, which may also include other donor segments as assigned. This encompasses personalized impact reports, acknowledgment letters, correspondence, touchpoints, invitations and other necessary communication. Work closely with the Division of University Advancement Communications team on projects as needed, including donor stories, publicity, one-off recognition pieces and reports. Donor Experience and Hospitality Mange the planning and execution of high-touch donor experiences, including athletic suite hospitality, special events, donor visits, gift celebrations and other customized engagement opportunities, ensuring premium hospitality, meaningful engagement, unique experiences and stewardship of high-level donors. Manage the selection, procurement and distribution of unique donor gifts, ensuring high-quality, personalized items that align with the donor engagement strategies. Organize and execute timely, meaningful follow-up after donor experiences and engagements, ensuring continued engagement with the principal gifts team and development officers. This position requires availability for some evenings and weekends to support donor experiences and events, including athletic hospitality. Some travel may be required for off-campus donor experiences or professional conferences. Administrative Tasks Maintain accurate and up-to-date records of donor interactions, preferences, stewardship plans, engagement plans and other information in the constituent management system. Utilize data to inform and enhance donor strategies. Document new departmental processes and procedures and update existing ones to ensure consistency and efficiency. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: post-high school education may substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) A valid Florida or Georgia Driver's License or the ability to obtain. Preferred Qualifications A preferred candidate will have 5+ years of previous experience in donor relations, annual giving or development activities in a nonprofit organization and have developed the skills needed to work with high-level donors and University Advancement leadership. Experience planning and executing high-level donor experiences, events or hospitality is preferred. Demonstrated ability to thrive in dynamic environments, effectively adapting to changing priorities with a flexible and proactive approach. This candidate will also have a strong attention to detail and excel at building and managing processes. Other Information Who is the ideal candidate for this position? You understand and enjoy the creative and data sides of advancement work and appreciate how important each is in donor relations. You have demonstrated project management skills, excellent interpersonal skills, exceptional verbal and written communication skills and a robust knowledge of donor relations. You have a proven record of successfully working with or managing high-level or principal donors and/or their stewardship plans. You enjoy creating thoughtful donor experiences and understand how hospitality, personalization and attention to detail can make an engagement meaningful. You are a strategic thinker looking to use your creativity and resourcefulness to make a difference. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63498&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Carpet Supervisor",
      "description": "Carpet Supervisor Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63498 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Custodial Services Responsibilities Supervises Custodial Staff. Provides training and instruction. Sets goals and objectives and determines workloads. Plans and establishes methods and frequency for cleaning. Communicates with the supervisory chain of command regarding daily operations and personnel-related matters. Prepares forms and investigates incidents of on-the-job accidents/injuries of employees. Maintains accurate and up-to-date daily attendance and leave records. Conducts general inspections of buildings for overall cleanliness and sanitation. Identifies deficiencies in cleaning and conducts follow-up inspections to ensure that corrective measures have been taken to bring cleaning up to established standards. Identifies and reports carpet cleaning or other maintenance needs as needed. Initiates work orders as necessary. Coordinates and schedules all special custodial projects within assigned building(s). Serves as liaison between custodial staff and other staff and Residential Student Experience Life Staff. Works closely and communicates with building occupants to ensure that custodial work does not disrupt operations. Provides quality customer service and promotes a positive working relationship between custodial staff and customers. Assists pest control services/walk through to address pest issues. Responsible for inventory control of custodial supplies and equipment. Issues supplies and equipment and ensures proper use. Inspects equipment and ensures proper maintenance and daily cleaning of carts, vacuums, floor machines, etc. Initiates work orders for carpet cleaning, maintenance, repairs, pest control, and other services that cannot be performed by custodial staff. Operates University-owned vehicles as necessary. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years' experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Relevant training may substitute for experience. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or ability to obtain upon hire. Preferred Qualifications Candidates with supervisory experience and two or more years of experience in carpet cleaning are strongly preferred. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=61131&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Faculty Psychologist (Two Positions) – Clinical Assistant Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Student Affairs/Admissions - Medicine)",
      "description": "Faculty Psychologist (Two Positions) – Clinical Assistant Professor, 12 Month Salaried (Student Affairs/Admissions - Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 61131 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Medicine, Student Affairs/Admissions Responsibilities The FSU College of Medicine (COM) Office of Student Counseling Services provides psychological and educational support services to graduate students in the Medicine, Physician Assistant, Bridge to Medicine, and Biomedical Sciences programs. The faculty psychologist will be responsible for providing individual therapy and personal counseling to matriculated students for general mental health concerns, adjustment disorders, personal stressors, and the promotion of well-being; for advising students and developing strategies to address academic deficiencies and to facilitate academic success; and for the initial evaluation, screening, and referral as appropriate of matriculated students for psychiatric care. All services are provided on-site in the FSU COM via in-person or telehealth scheduled appointments. As faculty, the incumbent will be expected to be active primarily in clinical service, and also smaller commitments in teaching and research consistent with the College of Medicine's mission. Qualifications Applicants must hold a doctoral degree from an American Psychological Association (APA)-approved counseling or clinical psychology program to include an APA-approved pre-doctoral internship and Florida licensure as a psychologist, or eligibility to obtain within 90 days of employment. Preferred Qualifications At least two years of experience in counseling or clinical psychology, with a minimum of one year of post-doctoral clinical experience in individual and group counseling. Strong oral and written communication skills. Preference given to candidates with postdoctoral work experience with college students or with young adults in a health science setting and/or experience providing academic support services. Doctorate level training in the science of learning, including educational psychology or school psychology. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for the role? This role is ideal for a team-oriented candidate looking for an opportunity to work in-person in a small office in a collaborative environment. The candidate must enjoy and be passionate about providing clinical services to the graduate student population, which includes not only therapy services but also academic support services, as well as becoming immersed in the best practices in medical education and support. What is a typical day? A typical day primarily involves provision of direct service (academic and/or mental health support) to College of Medicine graduate students in individual appointments in the Psychologist's private office. Some group services may be provided in either an academic or therapy context. In this role, you will work with a small team of other licensed psychologists, with regular consultation available, as well as full-time administrative support staff. There are no expectations on-call, evening, or weekend work, and the office observes all University-wide holidays, breaks, and closures. This faculty position also includes a small percentage (5-10%) of scholarly and teaching responsibilities, which are carefully balanced with a manageable client caseload. Contact Info Taylor Thompson, Ph.D. 850/644-0492 | tlthompson@admin.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range This position is expected to offer a salary in the range of $95,000 – $105,000; however, final compensation will be determined based on experience and qualifications. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://hr.fsu.edu/facultyjobs. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The job opening serves to recruit for two non-tenure earning positions. There is no remote work option for these positions. This job opening is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63809&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Systems Analyst",
      "description": "Financial Aid Systems Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63809 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Financial Aid Responsibilities The Division of Enrollment Management is comprised of four distinct units: Office of Admissions, Office of the University Registrar, Office of Financial Aid, and Technology Operations. Enrollment Management’s integrated services provide distinctive support throughout the students’ development and progression in their academic experience – from recruitment through commencement. Through collaboration, communication, and commitment, all units within Enrollment Management achieve the highest level of student-centered service to current and prospective students and families as well as to campus partners across the University. The Technology Operations Unit within Enrollment Management provides technology support, technology-based solutions, systems configuration, identity and data management, and analysis across the division. The unit works closely with subject matter experts in Admissions, Registrar, and Financial Aid to meet the operational and reporting needs of various stockholders across campus. Analyzes and monitors new and evolving technologies to improve business processes; assesses business processes and makes recommendations to improve and enhance the same through the implementation of technology solutions; documents business processes, conducts testing and training of staff; addresses informational needs, assists in the development of functional specifications and collaborates with the Senior Assistant Director to ensure adequate testing of processes and troubleshoot issues; documents system security processes and assists in conducting regular security reviews and makes recommendations for functional enhancements. Leads the evaluation, testing, troubleshooting and deployment of changes to functional operations. Analyzes, evaluates and determines financial aid awarded to students; performs business functions for all sections in the Office of Financial Aid. Conducts detailed analysis and works with systems group to develop enhancements as needed to ensure compliance with Federal, State and Institutional policy. Serves as liaison with ITS and other campus stakeholders in the implementation and training of new technologies that are being implemented in the university, some of these technologies include but not are not limited to CRM, Document Management and a seamless workflow system; assists in identifying the needs of the office as related to the systematic processing of federal, state and institutional data for the awarding of aid to students. Makes recommendation to integrate and implement a friendly consumer service process. Collects and analyzes system data for the department. Responsible for research and interpretation of federal, state and institutional regulations relating to student financial aid by formulating, developing and revising policies and procedures to ensure compliance as well as compatibility with federal, state and institution regulations. Counsels and advises students, parents and public on Financial Aid. Creates custom reports based on functional needs, provides operational data for decision making, and designs solutions to provide data in the appropriate format as required, trains users in technical processes related to financial aid processing. This position will also assist with quality assurance checks, special projects and surveys. Monitors the electronic information services for the Office of Financial Aid. Assists in designing and developing training for Financial Aid staff and related offices regarding computer-based informational portal and financial aid systems processing. Analyzes system security, collects and produces reports of data. Develops analytical s capabilities for the Office of Financial Aid to assist senior management with decision making on processes such as packaging and fund allocations. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications A bachelor's degree and two years of experience in enrollment services. Ability to multi-task within a fast-paced work environment. Experience implementing and/or supporting a new initiatives (policy, technology, procedure, etc.). Experience with interactive visualization software. Strong organizational, analytical, and communication skills desired. Previous experience and comfort working with a variety of computer software applications, databases, and student information systems (PeopleSoft). Ability to manage multiple projects and responsibilities at the same time. Prior experience analyzing data to create reports, to identify trends and to make decisions University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $50,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63663&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Grants Administrator for Research & Science - College of Nursing, Office for Research & Scholarship",
      "description": "Grants Administrator for Research & Science - College of Nursing, Office for Research & Scholarship Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63663 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University College of Nursing Office for Research & Scholarship (ORS) Responsibilities Reports directly to the Assistant Director for the College of Nursing (CON) Office of Research. Will support the college’s research team, but will be primarily responsible for development, implementation, and monitoring of the administration of contract/grant activity for an assigned portfolio. Processes and provides guidance on sponsored project HR, Purchasing and Travel transactions. Responsible for oversight of the post-award contract/grant activities. Responsible for developing and preparing financial reports, tracking salary commitments, identifying and resolving funding and compliance issues, coordinating close-outs; documents organization and storage. Advises and assists faculty, staff, and principal investigators in all areas of contracts/grant pre-award activities. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to eight years. This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification , or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications The preferred candidate will have experience in research administration, grants and contracts management, financial reporting, and sponsored project compliance, preferably within a higher education or a research institution. Candidates should demonstrate the ability to manage pre-award and post-award activities, including preparing and reviewing grant proposals, developing budgets, tracking salary commitments, reconciling financial data, monitoring expenditures, resolving funding discrepancies, and coordinating project closeouts. Familiarity with federal, state, and private funding sources, including National Institutes of Health (NIH) guidelines and other sponsor requirements, is preferred. The ideal candidate will possess strong analytical and organizational skills, with the ability to interpret and apply institutional policies, sponsor regulations, and compliance requirements to ensure accurate and timely submissions and reporting. Experience developing financial reports, analyzing project spending, projecting salary allocations, identifying funding opportunities, and supporting strategic planning initiatives is highly desirable. Candidates should also demonstrate proficiency in developing administrative procedures, establishing departmental deadlines, maintaining organized documentation, and managing multiple projects simultaneously. Strong written and verbal communication skills are essential, as the position requires collaboration with faculty, principal investigators, departmental leadership, funding agencies, the Research Foundation, and other sponsored research stakeholders. The ability to build effective working relationships, provide guidance on sponsored project administration, and support staff through training and mentoring is also preferred. A bachelor's degree and four years of relevant experience, or an equivalent combination of postsecondary education and experience. Familiarity with financial management systems, budgeting practices, contract administration, and applicable computer applications is highly desirable. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62924&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "IT Support Specialist",
      "description": "IT Support Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62924 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU’s Department of Information Technology Services (ITS) Responsibilities The Florida State University Physics Department IT group is a small, three-person team supporting a department whose IT needs span everything from standard office and classroom support to custom hardware builds, computational clusters, and specialized research instrumentation. The work is varied, the environment is collaborative, and no two weeks look the same. This position serves as an IT generalist for the research, teaching, and administrative missions of the Physics Department. Using strong skills in Linux/Unix office & research environments, provides computer support (hardware & software) for faculty, staff, students, and post-docs. Develops, installs, and supports Linux clusters including computational clusters. Assembles, installs, diagnoses and repairs computer systems at the component level. Performs preventive maintenance, hardware upgrades & software updates. Implements networking and security solutions for Linux, Macs and Windows workstations. Performs routine backups of systems and user-data. Supports the department's network infrastructure by identifying infected computers and resolving PC/workstation security matters. Supports server functions like DHCP, LDAP, routing, firewalls, clustering, email, wiki and web services. Installs and oversees the network security software on computers. Provides software support for all operating systems including Linux (Ubuntu, AlmaLinux, and openSUSE), macOS, and Windows, including drivers/utilities, office productivity suites/apps. Supports the installation of physics instructional-laboratories' apps/utilities, data visualization software, data acquisition software, symbolic mathematical packages, and programming languages. Installs and supports printing and copying functions on Windows/Macs/Linux workstations to various printers and copiers. Maintains records and documentation as needed. Scrubs data off old PCs before repurposing/surplus. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree or a high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: or combination of high school education and experience equal to four years). Preferred Qualifications IT related degree would be a plus. Information/endpoint security Linux/Unix systems administration Scripting and automation (Bash, Python) Computational cluster operations Independent work and self-direction Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? The ideal candidate is a self-starter who takes ownership of problems and sees them through to resolution without close supervision. Equally comfortable working a helpdesk queue, tackling a Linux administration task, or explaining a technical issue to a faculty member in plain language. Strong critical thinking matters more here than a checklist of certifications — this environment rewards people who can figure things out, not just follow a runbook. What is a typical day in this position? There isn't one, and that's part of what makes this role a good fit for the right person. Depending on the time of semester, a day might be dominated by end-user support requests, or it might be largely project-driven work on infrastructure, systems, or professional development. Semester starts to end to be busier on the helpdesk side; mid-semester shifts toward longer-horizon work. Comfort with that variability is essential. What can I expect in the first 60-90 days? The first 60-90 days will focus on getting oriented — learning the environment, the people, and the existing infrastructure. Beyond that, the specific work that takes shape will depend on what is in motion at the time of hire. The honest answer is that it depends on timing, ongoing projects, and departmental need. What remains constant is direct access to a manager and a team that supports its members throughout the onboarding process. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62975&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Pre-Law Academic Advisor (Multiple Vacancies)",
      "description": "Pre-Law Academic Advisor (Multiple Vacancies) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62975 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Advising First – Division of Undergraduate Studies Responsibilities Serves as a Pre-Law Academic Advisor for undergraduate students and discusses topics including but not limited to exploring the field of law, excelling in the first year, exploring majors, engaging in experiential learning. Supports students by reviewing documents (e.g., resumes, personal statements, and other writing samples), application timelines and school selection, and assisting with law school financial planning. Maintains detailed advising notes in university database and participates in pre-law outreach and programming initiatives as instructed by the Pre-Law Assistant Director. Completes all corresponding administrative tasks associated with the position. Teaches multiple sections of pre-law courses, and develops and revises course syllabi, assignments, and course materials. Mentors and oversees undergraduate pre-law peer leaders, their programming development and execution, as well as any other tasks leaders complete related to the pre-law experience overall. Reviews pre-law student engagement and outcomes data using available tools (e.g., Admissions, EAB, Pre-Law listserv, Nole Network, and LSAC Advisor Portal). Creates outreach campaigns in EAB to encourage timely participation with pre-law advising. Presents pre-law campus networking presentations to students during orientation sessions and other campus events. Provides ongoing education and updates on law school admission trends as well as stays up to date on policies and changes impacting students applying to law school. Attends regional or national conferences (e.g., PLANC or SAPLA) to stay current on industry best practices. Qualifications Master's degree and four years of experience. Preferred Qualifications Experience in roles such as advising, coaching, or other student services. Ability to extract complex academic information from various sources and maintain confidentiality. Experience and/or working knowledge of student advising, counseling, or working one-on-one with people in a professional or academic setting. Creative problem-solving skills. Experience with Microsoft Office and ability to learn the Advising system. Ability to interpret and explain policies, procedures, goals, and objectives to students, parents, faculty, and staff. Ability to prioritize, organize, and perform multiple work assignments simultaneously with minimal to moderate supervision. Ability to deal with people in a calm, confident manner and with complete objectivity. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships with students, parents, supervisors, and interdepartmental personnel. Attention to detail with a high standard of integrity. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $50,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
