    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63772&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Research Grants Administration - Dean's Office",
      "description": "Director of Research Grants Administration - Dean's Office Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63772 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is seeking a highly motivated and experienced professional to serve as the Director of Research Grant Administration. Responsibilities About This Role The Director of Research & Grants Administration plays a vital role in the administrative direction of the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. The Director will participate in strategic planning within the Joint College, related to financial operations and aligning the challenges of the joint college structure with university-wide impact. Why This Role Matters The management, staffing, and coordination of Contract and Grant (C&G) financial activities within the Joint College is critical to the College's growing research portfolio. By building partnerships across FAMU and FSU, and with public and private organizations, this position will advance the Joint College's research mission through supporting faculty and enhancing research compliance. What You Will Do This position is responsible for interpreting, providing guidance, and creating Joint College research procedures to align with both FAMU and FSU C&G policies. The selected candidate will participate in C&G policy development by implementing policies and procedures essential for sound and effective fiscal management of the Joint College. The position will also: Develop long-term C&G financial forecasts. Serve as the liaison between the Joint College and university areas such as Sponsored Research, Budget, Procurement, Controller, Foundation, and Travel offices within both institutions (FAMU and FSU). Serve as the C&G financial point of contact in the absence of the Assistant Dean for Administration. Serve as the primary contact on behalf of the College for annual C&G audits and national accreditation reporting. Provide C&G financial advice and financial administrative counsel to Joint College administrators and Principal Investigators (PI). Oversee post-award management for the Joint College including C&G financial monitoring, salary commitments, cost share tracking, compliance review, and project close-outs. Develop and maintain C&G financial and technical reports and budget projections, and resolve funding and compliance issues. Ensure grants compliance team schedules and conducts regular meetings with assigned PIs to review award spend status and obligations. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree and six years of experience related to budget, financial, and/or accounting services or a high school diploma or equivalent and ten years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to ten years) This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of The Uniform Administrative Requirements, Cost Principles, and Audit Requirements for Federal Awards (\"Uniform Guidance\"). Knowledge of contract administration in a grants setting. Knowledge of public and private grants awards. Knowledge of and ability to apply Generally Accepted Accounting Principles (GAAP). University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
