      "title": "Generator Technician (Levels 1-2)",
      "description": "Generator Technician (Levels 1-2) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62619 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Facilities - Maintenance Responsibilities Performs scheduled maintenance and repairs on the University emergency power supply system. Ensures that all are operational by performing periodic tests on generators, automatic transfer switches, annunciator panels, and associated components. Conducts load test per NFPA requirements. Performs scheduled maintenance and repairs on the University emergency supplies (primarily diesel cycle prime movers), including but not limited to, battery chargers, coolant flush, oil change, oil filter, air filter, fuel filter, etc. Maintains necessary supplies to handle emergency situations. Operates University vehicles and performs other related work as required in support of Facilities Maintenance. Qualifications A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or ability to obtain upon hire. High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. Anticipated Salary Range The anticipated starting salary is $37,400, commensurate with experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The work schedule is 8:00am to 4:30pm with a 30-minute break. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63018&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Machinist/Tool Maker (Physics)",
      "description": "Machinist/Tool Maker (Physics) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63018 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Physics I Florida State University Responsibilities Fabricates new equipment and modifies existing instrumentation to precision tolerances of up to 0.0001 inch, as required by research applications. Selects appropriate materials and manufacturing processes based on design, performance, and application requirements. Operates and maintains a broad range of Instrument Shop equipment used in the fabrication of research instrumentation, including CNC machining centers, CNC lathes, manual machine tools, and other precision fabrication equipment. From engineering drawings, verbal instructions, or conceptual sketches, fabricates highly complex research apparatus, instruments, components, and tooling. Utilizes Computer-Aided Design (CAD) software to produce technical drawings. Uses Computer-Aided Manufacturing (CAM) software to generate toolpaths and machine programs for various computer-controlled manufacturing equipment, including CNC milling machines, CNC lathes, and wire electrical discharge machining (Wire EDM) systems. Collaborates with faculty, scientists, researchers, and students to design and develop prototypes, scientific instrumentation, tooling, fixtures, and specialized research equipment. Develops manufacturing strategies and provides technical expertise throughout the design and fabrication process. Trains technical staff and other personnel in the programming, operation, and safe use of CNC machining centers, wire electrical discharge machining (Wire EDM) systems, and other advanced manufacturing equipment. Collaborates with faculty and instructional staff to design, develop, fabricate, and support classroom laboratory experiments, instructional apparatus, and lecture demonstration equipment for Physics and Astronomy courses. Diagnoses and repairs scientific and instructional instrumentation. Maintains required safety training and certifications and ensures compliance with applicable university, state, and federal safety policies and procedures. Responsible for the safe operation, maintenance, and stewardship of Physics Instrument Shop equipment. Performs routine preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, calibration, and repair of machine tools and fabrication equipment to ensure reliable operation and minimize downtime. Maintains anodizing, surface finishing, and other plating systems as needed, ensuring compliance with applicable environmental, health, and safety regulations and established operating procedures. Qualifications Bachelor's degree; or a high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated starting salary for the position is in the mid-$40,000s to mid-$50,000s. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62737&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Maintenance Support Worker (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Maintenance Support Worker (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62737 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Finance and Administration Department About Us | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Assists with maintenance of buildings, including windows, doors, furnishings, drywall, painting, construction, trash and debris removal, and cleaning of all areas; provides set-ups for special functions both on and off campus. Performs general cleaning and grounds maintenance around buildings, parking areas, drives, and other campus areas; operates mowers, edgers, fertilizer spreaders, spray rig, tractor, and weed trimmer as necessary to maintain law areas; plants trees, maintains roadways, parking areas, and fencing. Maintains exterior sprinkler systems, makes repairs to water pipes and sprinkler heads. Performs routine maintenance of all groundskeeping equipment, mowers, tractors, edgers, other lawn equipment, and tools. Assists in HVAC routine preventive maintenance, special projects, emergency repairs, cleaning, adjusting of machinery, cleaning equipment rooms; assists in repair of piping for water and sewer systems; assists in other duties as directed by supervisor. Qualifications Completion of 9th grade. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Knowledge of general safety practices (OSHA awareness). OSHA 10 or 30 certification. Trade-related certifications (entry-level HVAC, electrical, or plumbing). Helpful During the first three months, the Maintenance Support Worker will receive structured, hands-on training to build familiarity with campus systems, tools, and safety procedures. The selected candidate will work closely with their supervisor and department head to: Participate in guided training sessions on university equipment, facilities, and standard operating procedures. Shadow experienced staff to learn daily workflows and preventative maintenance practices. Gain an understanding of department safety protocols and compliance requirements. Take on progressively more independent assignments with ongoing support and feedback. Establish strong working relationships with team members and campus partners. By the end of the first 90 days, the Maintenance Support Worker is expected to be confident in navigating campus facilities, performing routine maintenance tasks, and contributing independently to the department's work while continuing to develop advanced skills. Contact Info Inquiries should be directed to David Gary at dgary@fsu.edu f or more information regarding this position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about our university and campuses. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our interactive too l to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply to Florida State University at https://jobs.fsu.edu. If you are a current FSU employee, apply via myFSU > Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for eligibility information and required documentation , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is a Full-time USPS position. This position requires the successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position qualifies for on-call and shift differential pay. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63771&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Air-Sea Interaction (OPS)",
      "description": "Postdoctoral Scholar in Air-Sea Interaction (OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63771 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Earth, Ocean and Atmospheric Science I College of Arts & Sciences Responsibilities The postdoctoral researcher will be part of a NOAA-funded project investigating air-sea interaction in the Gulf Stream region. The project is a collaborative effort with the University of Rhode Island. The candidate is expected to conduct independent, high-quality research, including the publication of papers and presentation of work at conferences both nationally and internationally. The postdoctoral researcher will also work collaboratively with the University of Rhode Island. Qualifications A PhD in physical oceanography, air-sea interaction, atmospheric science or closely related field is required. Proficiency with data analysis. Strong verbal and written communication skills. Ability to work effectively within an interdisciplinary team. Contact Info Informal inquiries should be made to Rhys Parfitt . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary commensurate with experience and qualifications. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Final candidate will be asked to provide the names of two references. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . The appointment is initially for one year, with the possibility of an extension based on funding and acceptable performance. This position is being advertised as open-until-filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63773&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Preventative Maintenance Technician 1",
      "description": "Preventative Maintenance Technician 1 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63773 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities Maintenance Department Responsibilities Performs daily, weekly, monthly, semi and annual preventive maintenance on all HVAC, plumbing, electrical, fire systems, ice machines, blue light emergency call stations, roofing, building envelopes, and automated external defibrillator equipment within the assigned area. This includes but not limited to cleaning, servicing and inspecting various types of HVAC Systems: including, but not limited to, cleaning of cooling and heating coils on a scheduled cycle; replacement and adjustments of pulley drive belts, pulleys and bearings; service to blower wheel assemblies and lubrication of all components; filter changing and service to all related equipment within a HVAC system. Performs maintenance and repairs on major equipment as required. Other related work as assigned. Responsible for and operates departmental vehicle as assigned. Climbs ladders, works in confined/tight spaces and work with various chemicals using proper PPE as it pertains to the work environment. Completes required safety training and complies with all safety standards including, but not limited to: lock out-tag out, ladders, aerial lifts, confined space safety, safe handling of hazardous chemicals, participation in campus safety teams, and wearing required personal protective equipment (PPE). Reports complex and/or unusual problems to the supervisor and coordinates with other Maintenance staff as required to complete complex tasks. Perform preventive maintenance, troubleshooting, and repairs to plumbing systems. Duties include repairing faucets, valves, pipes, drains (including unclogging), toilets, and other plumbing related items. Completes required safety training and complies with all safety standards including, but not limited to: lock out-tag out, safe handling of refrigerant, confined space safety, safe handling of hazardous chemicals, participation in campus safety teams, and wearing required personal protective equipment (PPE). Reports complex and/or unusual problems to the supervisor and coordinates with other Maintenance staff as required to complete complex tasks. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent and two years' experience or a post high school education and experience equal to two years, or a relevant Technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. Ability to meet the physical demands of this position to include climbing ladders and working in confined/tight spaces. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63755&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Technical Production Assistant (OPS/Part-Time)",
      "description": "Technical Production Assistant (OPS/Part-Time) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63755 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Technical and production assistance for Art of Performance and On Screen productions; work with Production Manager to assist as production crew during load in, technical and dress rehearsals, and performances/film screenings; assist artists/designers as much as possible on implementation of design; act as liaison between Production Manager and guest artists and rental productions to troubleshoot; communicate as needed with Box Office and Front of House for Historic Asolo Theater; and act as production staff for evening and weekend productions in collaboration with Production Manager and Art Performance staff. Executes set build, load in and technical requirements as determined by Production Manager. Reads and interprets lighting plot and other drawings in association with the Production Manager. Runs light board for dress rehearsal and performances as needed. Runs preshow check to make sure all equipment is working prior to performances and film screenings, troubleshooting as needed. Works with IATSE electric crew. Maintains and repairs conventional fixtures, scrollers and moving lights. Operates of film projection system for testing and movie screenings. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent. Three years of professional theatre experience. Ability to lift and carry 60 pounds, climb ladders, and work at heights. Preferred Qualifications Bachelor's Degree in Technical Theater and two years of professional experience. Knowledge of: Fundamentals of electricity and general computer operation. Basic programming knowledge of ETC GIO lighting console. Basic knowledge of Q-Lab or similar. Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $20 to $25 per hour based on the education, skill, and experience of the selected candidate. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Work Location: Sarasota, FL Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Working Hours Average of 28 hours a week. Requires the ability to work evenings and weekends. Please note the working hours are dynamic and based on scheduled performances. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63749&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Lab Animal Technician",
      "description": "Assistant Lab Animal Technician Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63749 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Laboratory Animal Resources (LAR) seeks to fill an Assistant Animal Lab Technician Responsibilities Provides diligent and responsible animal care. Feeds and waters animals. Changes and cleans cages. Sanitizes equipment and facilities. Records and reports animal abnormalities including altered eating, drinking, waste elimination, behavior, superficial lesions, and/or death. Assists with technical procedures including record keeping, animal identification, breeding, sexing, specimen collection, preparing diets, and euthanasia. Records and reports environmental abnormalities. Performs routine duties associated with cage sanitation and preparation for reuse in a research setting including cage maintenance, monitoring equipment for proper function and maintaining sanitary conditions. Operates mechanical washers and ensures cage washing and related equipment are in proper working order. Performs routine start-up and shut down procedures. Operates autoclaves to sterilize or decontaminate caging and equipment. Assists in receiving and storing materials, food, and supplies. Transports animals, caging, and supplies between animal rooms and facilities, requiring a valid Driver's License and the ability to lift up to 50 lbs. Provides routine physical maintenance of assigned areas Maintains sanitary condition of cage wash facilities and other ancillary areas including corridors and storage rooms. May assist in training other LAR personnel. Requires understanding and compliance with departmental and institutional policies and procedures, as well as, other applicable federal and state regulations. Performs other duties as assigned as it relates to the LAR operations. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years experience or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to two years. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at RSCH-WorkForce@fsu.edu FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
