      "title": "Incubator Research Facilities Lead",
      "description": "Incubator Research Facilities Lead Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63776 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department IGNITE Tallahassee is looking to fill the role of its Incubator Research Facilities Lead. Responsibilities This position serves as the primary technical resource for IGNITE incubator companies operating within the program. Advises resident companies on laboratory capabilities for their product development and R&D. Conducts consultative meetings with current and prospective members to assess research and equipment needs and to scope how laboratory resources can support company goals. Connects resident clients with specialized technical services and scientific instrumentation available through FSU core facilities and research partners. Is r esponsible for management of the shared research laboratory facilities supporting IGNITE and affiliated research members and clients. Evaluates and identifies equipment needs to keep pace with clients’ research demands. Establishes and manages the maintenance, safety, and service program for research equipment, including negotiation of service contracts and vendor relationships. Oversees day-to-day shared lab operations—including preventative maintenance and servicing scientific instrumentation across IGNITE-managed and affiliated research space, including but not limited to chemical fume hoods and exhaust systems, tissue culture cabinets, autoclaves, centrifuges, and cold storage refrigeration up to -80*C. Establishes policies and procedures governing shared lab usage, storage, and space allocation to optimize the research environment for multiple concurrent member projects. Maintains and upkeeps shared instrumentation, use training, usage schedule, and client customer service. Responsible for keeping records up-to-date that pertain to certification, client use logs, safety testing. Establishes and maintains Biosafety Level 2 compliance for IGNITE-managed labs. Ensures client personnel are trained and oriented appropriately for their research workflow and up to biosafety standards. Identifies and mitigates safety and regulatory risk to ongoing research activity; maintains safety and compliance documentation. Coordinates with FSU EHS and Biosafety personnel on regulatory compliance matters. Directs proper handling, packaging, labeling, and documentation of lab and hazardous waste in coordination with appropriate contractors. Recruits, trains, and supervises student interns and OPS laboratory assistants supporting the research program, assigning duties and overseeing their development as research support staff. Qualifications Master's degree and 4 years’ direct experience in managing laboratory or specialized facilities (e.g. bio manufacturing, scale-up engineering, etc.). Preferred Qualifications Our preferred candidate would hold a Master’s degree or Ph.D. and have experience with biosafety protocols, GMP standards, and/or lab and hazardous waste management. Experience managing user facilities, core facilities, manufacturing facilities, or engineering/bio startup incubator facilities highly desired. Contact Info Cassidy Cooksey at rsch-workforce@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
