      "title": "Events Assistant",
      "description": "Events Assistant Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63768 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department College of Law Responsibilities As part of the Faculty Support Office, this position works closely with the Event Manager and helps plan, organize, and promote outreach and informational events; assists with Faculty/Program events; provides administrative, clerical & instructional support to faculty as needed; and provides exam support . Assists with faculty events, including reserving rooms for events and booking guest travel. Orders catering, generates graphics & media for posting, and creates an RSVP link. Must coordinate tech needs and make signage as needed. May attend the weekly event planning meetings. Events include (but not limited to): Collegewide Events, Enrichment Speakers, Summer Presentation Series, Distinguished Environmental Lecture, Legal Writing Workshops, Clinic events, etc. Assist with preparing the monthly staff newsletter, preparing and updating forms, staff phone list, staff photos, and assisting with other admin activities and special projects. Ensures all new employees are added to contact lists, websites, and directories. Ensures the effective operation of the Faculty Support Office's daily operations: Greets visitors to the Faculty Support Office; Communicates regularly with faculty, deans, guests, and judges; Manages mail delivery to Adjunct Faculty. Monitors, updates, and maintains all designated bulletin boards, including ensuring faculty publication display cases and room signage are current. Ensures that all notices, materials, and announcements are up to date and displayed in an aesthetically pleasing manner. Provides back-up support to other staff for travel authorizations and Canvas course entry. Assists with exam administration each semester and orders lunches for exam staff. Required to have both a travel and a purchasing card and to be fully trained on both. Must be familiar with CANVAS, OSCAR, and FEAS. Provides rosters, creates add/drop sheets, attendance and seating charts; tracks attendance for all classes and reports monthly to the Associate Dean of Student Affairs. May provide clerical assistance to faculty as requested/assigned. Qualifications High School diploma or equivalency and four years of experience, or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to four years. Contact Info Janine Welch, College of Law Associate Dean for Administration jwelch@law.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63740&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Art - Foundations)",
      "description": "Teaching Faculty I, 9 Month Salaried (Department of Art - Foundations) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63740 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Art Responsibilities The position has responsibilities that include teaching undergraduate courses and service within the Department, College, University, and broader community. Primary teaching responsibilities include instruction in at least four areas of the Foundations Program: Two-Dimensional Foundations, Three-Dimensional Foundations, Drawing Foundations, Digital Foundations, and Contemporary Art & Design Foundations. The teaching load for this position is 3|3 per academic year. Participation in Program and Departmental service is required, including mentoring and advising students, as well as College, University, and broader community service, as appropriate. The position provides opportunities for curriculum development within the Foundations Program. Teaching upper-level or graduate courses outside of the Foundations Program may occasionally be available. Qualifications The position requires an MFA in Studio Art or a related field. Candidates should demonstrate excellence in teaching, strong communication and collaboration skills, and an understanding of a wide range of curricular and artistic methodologies. Candidates should also demonstrate broad knowledge and experience in 2D, 3D, and digital studio practices appropriate to teaching across the Foundations curriculum, as well as knowledge of the history, criticism, and theories of visual art. Preferred qualifications include demonstrated knowledge and experience with digital fabrication and digital design tools. Candidates should have an active studio practice, with emerging or established engagement in the field through exhibitions or other professional activities. Other Information The Department of Art in the College of Fine Arts at Florida State University seeks candidates for a 9-month Specialized Faculty position in our Foundations Program. The Department of Art confers BA, BFA, and MFA (3-year) Studio Art degrees. Our top-ranked programs encourage interdisciplinary investigations across a wide range of concentrations spanning Painting + Drawing, Photography + Moving Image, Printmaking + Book Arts, Sculpture + Expanded Media, and Ceramics. The department currently employs 22 full-time faculty. Florida State University College of Fine Arts is committed to building a meaningful community that values each person based on their distinctive and unique identity. The Department of Art strives to prepare students to imaginatively re-envision the world around us through critical inquiry. Contact Info Questions may be directed to the Search Committee chair, Liz Di Donna , Teaching Faculty II. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. For consideration, please submit the following: Letter of interest Curriculum Vitae Teaching philosophy A portfolio with 10-20 examples of student work A portfolio with 10-20 examples of your research Names and contact information for three references Optional submission materials: Sample syllabi Research statement Candidates selected to advance in the search process will be asked to provide three letters of reference. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Priority consideration will be given to completed applications submitted before December 1, 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63761&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Administrative Specialist (Finance & Administration - College of Medicine)",
      "description": "Administrative Specialist (Finance & Administration - College of Medicine) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63761 Location Hybrid Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine - Administrative Services The Office of MED Administrative Services provides centralized administrative support, operational leadership, and expertise to the academic departments and programs within the Florida State University College of Medicine. Working collaboratively with faculty, staff, departmental leadership, and College and University administration, the office supports a broad range of functions, including recruitment and employment actions, faculty development and advancement, position description/salary change administration, personnel reporting, regulatory compliance, and organizational operations. Through consistent processes, data-informed decision-making, and a commitment to service excellence, MED Administrative Services promotes operational efficiency, accuracy, compliance, and alignment with the strategic priorities of the College and the University. Responsibilities Serve as a primary administrative resource for assigned departments, building effective working relationships and coordinating faculty and staff employment processes. Processes, tracks, and documents position and salary-related transactions including salary adjustments, position updates, incentives, sign-on bonuses, and other approved actions. Supports faculty development and advancement processes, including appointments, evaluations, promotion and tenure, reappointments, post-tenure reviews. Coordinates and tracks personnel transactions, including recruitment, hiring, onboarding, funding changes, and separations. Maintains and reconciles personnel records across University and College systems to ensure accuracy, compliance, and timely processing. Assist with FACET, Assignment of Responsibility (AOR), instructor funding, and other faculty and administrative reporting requirements. Supports process improvements, special projects, and the development of standardized administrative procedures. Collaborates with departments, College leadership, and University offices to resolve administrative issues and promote responsive, consistent service delivery. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Experience in human resources administration, employment processes, faculty development and advancement processes, or related administrative functions, preferably in higher education. Strong organizational, communication, interpersonal, and problem-solving skills, with a commitment to service excellence. Demonstrated ability to build and maintain effective working relationships, collaborate across departments, and support a variety of stakeholders. Experience maintaining, reviewing, and reconciling personnel or administrative data to ensure accuracy and compliance. Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications, particularly Excel, and experience with SharePoint or similar collaboration platforms. Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, meet deadlines, and maintain accuracy and attention to detail. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and adapt to changing priorities in a collaborative environment. Helpful The FSU College of Medicine Administrative Services seeks a collaborative, detail-oriented, and service-focused Administrative Specialist to support faculty development and advancement processes, employment administration, reporting, compliance, and process improvement activities. This position works closely with departments and College leadership to coordinate administrative processes, interpret University policies, maintain records, and support the College's academic and administrative mission. Contact Info Selin S. Oliver | Program Director, MED Administrative Services University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting salary: Low to mid $40,000’s, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is based in Tallahassee, FL and is eligible for a hybrid work schedule. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63762&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Clinical Finance Director | Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc.",
      "description": "Clinical Finance Director | Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc. Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63762 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU College of Medicine | Florida Medical Practice Plan 1115 W Call St Tallahassee, FL 32304 Responsibilities The Clinical Finance Director serves as the critical bridge between FSU MED Finance & Administration, FMPP Clinical Operations, and FSU MED/FMPP Executive Leadership by directing the financial planning and analysis functions to support the strategic objectives of Florida Medical Practice Plan, Inc. Financial Planning/Budgeting/Forecasting: Direct the financial planning and analysis function for FMPP, Inc. clinical operations. Develop annual operating budgets and periodic financial forecasts for multiple practices and service lines. Evaluate revenue, expenses, profitability, provider productivity, and practice performance Strategic Financial Analysis/Decision Support: Provide executive clinical financial leadership using financial modeling, business case analyses. ROI studies, etc. Prepare executive reports, dashboards, presentations, & performance analyses that support data-engaged leadership decision-making Operational & Practice Performance Analytics: Lead the collection, validation, and analysis of operational and financial data to evaluate KPIs. Identify financial risks, operational inefficiencies, and emerging trends while recommending corrective actions and opportunities for performance improvement. Data Management, Reporting Systems and Business Intelligence: Oversee the development and maintenance of reporting tools, databases, dashboards, etc. for FMPP clinical operations. Ensure the integrity, accuracy, and consistency of financial and operational data utilized throughout FMPP. Utilize business intelligence platforms and reporting technologies to improve access to actionable information. Operational Improvement & Financial Stewardship: Serve as the financial planning resource for multiple medical practices. Lead process improvement initiatives, reporting automation efforts, and workflow assessments to enhance efficiency. Support audits, financial reviews, and compliance with organizational financial policies and standards. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and six years of experience related to budget, financial and/or accounting services; or a high school diploma/equivalent and experience equal to ten years. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Preferred Qualifications Familiarity with Epic Electronic Health Records software platform. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Salary is commensurate with experience and education. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63739&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Dean/Director, Office of Accessibility Services",
      "description": "Assistant Dean/Director, Office of Accessibility Services Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63739 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Student Support & Transition Office of Accessibility Services 874 Traditions Way, Suite 108 Student Services Bldg Tallahassee, Fl 32304 (850) 644-9566 oas@fsu.edu Responsibilities Oversee the implementation and development of initiatives and programs for students. Research and assist with the development of corresponding policies and procedures relating to the provision of accommodations, ADA/ADAAA compliance, academic testing procedures, and current and innovative technologies. Advises and trains University departments on accessibility issues. Promotes and monitors compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act, the Americans with Disabilities Amendments Act and the Rehabilitation Act of 1973 as amended. Communicates program services and maintains a high level of contact with students, faculty, staff, and internal/external University constituents. Attends corresponding community and state meetings. Directly oversees the Office of Accessibility Services Main Office which include the OAS Testing Center and the OAS Assistive Technology Center. Provides departmental direction and resolves issues that arise within the department. Identifies and evaluates departmental personnel issues, staffing needs, structure, and facility and space needs. Supervises and directs the work of USPS, A&P, and OPS employees and completes performance evaluations as required. Manages and monitors OAS budgets. Researches, secures, and administers program funding from local, state, and federal sources. Disperses and reports expenditures. Collaborates with campus partners to seek and secure outside funding sources. Works in conjunction with the Department of Student Support & Transitions to promote campus resources. Reviews documentation and collaborates with students to develop an academic accommodation plan. Assists in planning, developing and implementing services for students with all types of disabling conditions including learning, ADHD, mental health, medical, mobility, hearing, visual, and others. Serves as a liaison between faculty and students. Keeps current and detailed case notes within the OAS student data management system. Dean on Duty responsibilities on a rotational basis. Each Assistant and Associate Dean of Students is required to serve as the \"Dean on Duty\". During this time, the employee is responsible for managing all after hours crisis management situations, and triage emergency situations requiring a response from student affairs. These responses include acting independently and representing student affairs and, in some cases the entire University during very sensitive crisis situations. Maintains various scholarship resources offered through the OAS. Coordinates promotion, application process, chairs the scholarship committee and prepares required reports. Serves as the ADA Coordinator for Students. Investigates student grievances related to the ADA and advises University administration on application of federal law and emerging cases specifically related to provision of accommodations, testing center environments, and compliance with implementation technology. Coordinates University student accommodations (including academic, housing, dietary, and transportation) including the development, implementation, and monitoring of appropriate policies, procedures and practices to ensure compliance with the Americans with Disability Act, the Americans with Disabilities Amendments Qualifications Bachelor's degree in counseling or related field and four years' experience. Preferred Qualifications Master's degree preferred Contact Info Shelley Ducatt Student Support & Transition Office of Accessibility Services 874 Traditions Way, Suite 108 Student Services Bldg Tallahassee, Fl 32304 (850) 644-9566 oas@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary will be between $74, 390 - $94,174, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63757&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Educational Talent Search - Assistant Director (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Educational Talent Search - Assistant Director (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63757 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Student Recruitment, Services, Advising, and Data Management: Oversees and participates in the recruitment of pre-collegiate students to enhance academic enrichment and improve access to postsecondary opportunities for targeted middle and high school students. This includes organizing, implementing, and monitoring individual and group activities and services. Mentors and advises program participants regarding educational planning, career development, postsecondary pathways, and understanding federal financial aid. Additionally, monitors and maintains the electronic student database (BLUMEN) to ensure data integrity, accurate documentation of participant services, and timely updates. The Assistant Director will also assist in the progress monitoring of objectives directly tied to high school seniors. Participant Assessment, Progress Monitoring, and School Collaboration: Assesses the academic and personal needs of Talent Search participants to support achievement of Educational Talent Search (ETS) program objectives. Maintains and reviews student data in preparation for the Annual Performance Report (APR) through transcript evaluations, student interviews, academic progress monitoring, and regular participant check-ins. Collaborates with key personnel at target schools to develop and implement service plans responsive to participant needs while monitoring progress toward high school graduation and college readiness. This includes reviewing completion of college preparatory coursework and monitoring the submission of college admissions, financial aid, and scholarship applications. Responsible for Program Leadership, Staff Support, and Program Coordination: assists the TRIO ETS Director in the overall coordination and implementation of program services and objectives. Supervises and supports TRIO Talent Search staff in daily operations, program planning, service delivery, professional development, federal TRIO training, and team meetings. The Assistant Director serves as a key member of the senior leadership team and helps ensure consistent, high-quality programming across all service areas. Assists in developing and maintaining partnerships throughout the University in order to obtain Talent Search goals. Assists with grant-related administrative responsibilities, such as monitoring program activities and deliverables, supporting compliance, reviewing program data, assisting with federal reporting, and ensuring services are implemented in accordance with grant objectives. Responsibilities also include coordinating educational enrichment activities and program events, assisting with supervising and transporting program participants during approved activities, and performing other duties necessary to support program goals and objectives. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience related to academic and/or student services or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years in the same. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with high school students. Prior experience supervising a team. Helpful The Assistant Director supports the implementation and delivery of Florida State University Panama City’s TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) Program across eight designated target counties. The position requires regular travel to participating middle and high schools throughout Bay County and the surrounding areas to provide academic guidance, college and career-readiness services, and post-secondary planning support. The Assistant Director collaborates with students, families, school personnel, community partners, and program staff to promote academic success, high school graduation, and postsecondary enrollment among TRIO-eligible students. Responsibilities include monitoring participant progress, tracking high school seniors, and documenting postsecondary enrollment outcomes to support program objectives and federal reporting requirements. This position requires flexibility including attending monthly staff meetings, quarterly professional-development at FSU PC and FSU, work occasional evenings, weekends, as well as overnight, and out of area travel, to support program activities including, college visits, educational enrichment activities, professional development, student workshops, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $51,500, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position requires occasional travel to Tallahassee, FL. This position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63751&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Educational Talent Search, Program Associate (Tallahassee, FL)",
      "description": "Educational Talent Search, Program Associate (Tallahassee, FL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63751 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Participant Records, Data & Program Compliance: Maintain participant files and databases; enter and verify demographic, eligibility, participation, academic, and service data; assist with documentation for the Annual Performance Report (APR); track missing records and forms; maintain confidentiality; and support accurate documentation of project services and outcomes. Recruitment, Enrollment & Participant Support: Assist coordinators with recruitment and outreach; process applications and eligibility documentation; communicate with students, families, and school partners; maintain recruitment and participation rosters; and support follow-up efforts to help the program meet funded participant targets. Assists with the planning, coordination, and implementation of Talent Search activities, including workshops, tutoring, and academic enrichment activities, college and career exploration, campus visits, enrichment experiences, and summer programming. Coordinates program logistics, including participant registration, permission forms, transportation arrangements, meals, program materials, and activity schedules. Helps communicate transportation schedules and other program information to students, families, schools, staff, and approved transportation providers. Provides on-site support for programming activities and helps maintain required participation and activity documentation. Communications & General Program Administration: Maintain calendars and program communications; prepare correspondence, reports, meeting materials, and program documents; assist with purchasing and supply tracking as assigned; participate in staff meetings and training; and perform other duties that support achievement of Talent Search objectives. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with high school students. Helpful The ETS Program Associate will provide administrative, operational, and programmatic support for the Federal TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) program by supporting the effective delivery of services to eligible middle and high school students by assisting with student recruitment and enrollment, maintaining accurate participant records, coordinating program activities and communications, and supporting data collection and documentation required for federal reporting and performance tracking. The program assistant may be required to collaborate with community partners to increase program awareness across the 8 target areas. The program associate may be required to work occasional evenings, weekends, some overnight, and out-of-area travel to support program activities, college visits, educational enrichment experiences, professional development, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $36,250, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position will be primarily located in Tallahassee, FL and requires occasional travel to Panama City, FL. The position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63758&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator (Gadsden County)",
      "description": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator (Gadsden County) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63758 Location Quincy, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Sponsored Programs Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay, and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand-new residential housing complex on campus, right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Oversees recruitment and provides direct services to program participants in alignment with federal TRIO Educational Talent Search (ETS) objectives. Provides middle and high school participants with academic enrichment, tutoring, mentoring, career exploration, college and post-secondary planning, financial aid information, and other college-readiness services through individual and group advising, workshops, student check-ins, and school-based events. Maintains regular communication with participants to encourage engagement and participation in program services. Plans, coordinates, and implements activities that support ETS program objectives, including academic and career workshops, test preparation, community service initiatives, college and career exposure, campus visits, and other educational enrichment experiences that promote high school completion and preparation for college, career, or trade/technical education. Participates in federal TRIO training and professional development provided by the university, department, and other approved organizations. Evaluates participants' academic and educational needs through transcript reviews, student check-ins, and collaboration with teachers, counselors, families, and other school personnel. Monitors participants’ progress toward high school graduation and postsecondary readiness, including completion of college-preparatory coursework and applications for college admissions, financial aid, and scholarships. Collaborates with target school personnel and community partners to connect students and families with appropriate resources and provides guidance on college costs and financial aid. Responsibilities also include assisting with supervising and transporting program participants during approved program activities and performing other duties necessary to support program goals and objectives. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Prior experience working with high school students. Helpful The student program coordinator will travel to middle and high schools within the Gadsden County region to provide academic support to students. The coordinator will work with students, families, school personnel, community partners, and program staff to increase the number of TRIO-eligible students who graduate from high school and pursue postsecondary education. The coordinator will be required to attend monthly staff meetings and quarterly professional-development at FSU PC and FSU, work occasional evenings, weekends, some overnight, and out-of-area travel to support program activities, college visits, educational enrichment experiences, professional development, and other approved program events. Contact Info Melinda Jones University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $44,056, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. This position will be primarily located in Gadsden County and requires occasional travel to Panama City, FL and Tallahassee, FL. This position will begin in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63752&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Educational Talent Search, Student Program Coordinator - Gulf County",
