    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63760&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Associate (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Program Associate (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63760 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Finance & Administration Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Supports PCC Finance & Administration, Police & Public Safety, and Facilities, Operations, and Maintenance. Enters facility-use requests and work orders; runs request and biweekly event-schedule queries; formats reports for the Director of F&A, Facility Use Coordinator, Maintenance Supervisor, and Switchboard. Manages the parking permit program. Enters requisitions as backup for Facilities, Operations, and Maintenance, and Police & Public Safety. Processes monthly P-Card reconciliations, certification reports, and department ledger reconciliations. Backs up card access, key requests, and deposit slips. Backs up travel for interviewees, guests, and employees: obtains Dean/Associate Dean approval, enters requests, books reservations, communicates policies and details, and submits expense reports. Processes contracts for departments; drafts contracts as needed. Coordinates and leads Panama City Campus training on contracts and travel. Backs up the campus Switchboard and Mail Center; assists with the Schedule of Classes; maintains flyers in elevators and on bulletin boards; represents F&A at SGC meetings and briefs the Director on relevant issues. Performs other duties as needed. Assists campus departments and maintains cross-training to cover absences or workflow surges. Supports payroll by reviewing timecards and verifying cost center reports. Qualifications A high school diploma or equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post high-school education and/or experience may substitute at a comparable rate.) Preferred Qualifications Ability to establish effective working relationships with various departments in order to provide accurate documentation. Effective customer service skills are a must. Ability to prioritize tasks and meet deadlines. Strong attention to detail to ensure invoices, procurement-cards, and travel are processed correctly and on time. Ability to multitask. Helpful During the first two months, the Program Associate will receive structured, hands-on training to build familiarity with university policies and procedures. The selected candidate will work closely with their supervisor to: Participate in guided training sessions on university departments, purchasing, work orders, etc. Shadow experienced staff to learn daily workflows and deadlines. Gain an understanding of department responsibilities and requirements. Take on progressively more independent assignments with ongoing support and feedback. Establish strong working relationships with team members and campus partners. By the end of the first 60 days, the Program Associate is expected to be working independently with training as needed, being familiar with the campus departments, budgets, and policies and procedures, contributing independently to the department while continuing to develop advanced skills. Contact Info Jackie Brodie University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $36,250, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will start in late Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63723&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Manager - The Graduate School",
      "description": "Program Manager - The Graduate School Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63723 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Graduate School Responsibilities The program manager for the Graduate Student Resource Center (GSRC) is responsible for managing the administrative and programmatic functions of the GSRC travel grant program. Further, the program manager will lead marketing for academic and professional development programming to current FSU graduate students. The program manager will also assist the Director with the implementation of the Center’s workshops and lead administrative support across the office. Manages the coordination of planning, and implementing for all GSRC marketing, media, and events, including the annual Graduate Student Resource Fair with GSRC staff and OPS staff. Liaises with other campus partners and supports campus partner events. Responsible for coordinating all GSRC event logistics, including room reservations, invitations, publicity, and materials preparation. Leads or assists in the creation of high-impact academic and professional development programming for doctoral student success. Leads or assists with colloquiums, workshops, or forums for graduate students. Works in close coordination with the GSRC’s Director to lead the GSRC travel grant program. Reviews and evaluates travel grant materials, provides notice to recipients of travel grants, conducts budget reconciliation in consultation with the Associate Dean, assists in travel grant policy development, develops related publicity for the travel grant program. Assists the GSRC Director and Student Success Analyst in the development and administration of GRSC event feedback surveys. Collects and compiles data related to GSRC programs and services. Designs and writes the GSRC annual report and develops related charts and figures. Leads administrative operations, including clerical and facility duties, supplies/inventory, and assists in the supervision of OPS staff. Supports programmatic fundraising efforts. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience related to academic and/or student services or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years in the same. Preferred Qualifications Ability to communicate effectively verbally and in writing. Ability to establish and maintain effective working relationships. Ability to perform basic mathematical calculations. Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related federal, state, and local laws, ordinances, rules and regulations. Knowledge of and ability to interpret and apply related University policies, procedures, principles, and practices. Knowledge of applicable computer applications and basic computer functions. Ability to maintain accurate records and retrieve files from active or archive sources. Basic filing practices; including numeric and alphabetic systems. Knowledge of office practices, procedures, and etiquette. Preferred Master's degree. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Mid to upper $40,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63753&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Real Time Crime Center Analyst",
      "description": "Real Time Crime Center Analyst Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63753 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Public Safety Responsibilities The Real Time Crime Center Analyst performs work receiving, abstracting, and summarizing data pertaining to criminal activities and involves the preparation of crime analysis information, criminal intelligence gathering, and real-time patrol support. Real-Time Crime Analysis specialization includes research, assembling, and presentation of information to provide investigative leads and functional patterns to be used as situational awareness in real time. Collect, evaluate, and summarize criminal intelligence data, determining its significance, completeness, and usefulness. Ensure the collection, integrity, accuracy, and timely updating of data from a variety of sources. Review daily bulletins (BOLOs, teletypes, etc.) and shift reports and maintain accurate records. Read and comprehend criminal justice laws, legal codes, court procedures, precedents, government regulations, executive orders, and agency policies and procedures. Analyze police data and provide strategic interpretation of information received through computer-aided dispatch (CAD), telephone, radio, and other communication systems. Request and receive confidential information, interpret maps to assist in locating geographic areas, and provide timely intelligence support during active calls for service and field operations. Communicate information clearly, concisely, and accurately. Adhere to the agency's core values and professionally represent the organization. Establish and maintain effective working relationships with partner agencies, organization members, and the public while providing professional customer service. Report to work reliably and on schedule, plan and coordinate work assignments, and communicate effectively both verbally and in writing. Perform all assigned duties safely and effectively without posing a direct threat to the health or safety of others in the workplace. Meet requirements and maintain required licensures and certifications, as well as successful completion of agency-required training. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and two years of experience related to criminal intelligence, crime analysis, or military intelligence, or similarly analytical in nature. Relevant experience can be substituted on a year-to-year basis for the required education. A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Contact Info Malia Brown - (850) 644-1239 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Real Time Crime Center Analysts work a 12-hour shift schedule that follows a rotating long-week/short-week format. Work hours may be adjusted during the training period. This position is located at the Real-Time Crime Center (RTCC) in Innovation Park. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63748&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Social Sciences Librarian, 12 Month Salaried",
      "description": "Social Sciences Librarian, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63748 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Libraries Responsibilities The Social Sciences Librarian serves as the library liaison for Public Administration & Policy, Political Science, and International Affairs providing research and instructional support to faculty and students. The position supports access to government publications, data, and information resources through FSU's participation in the Federal Depository Library Program and oversees the Libraries' government information collections and specialist staff. Working closely with fellow Social and Behavioral Sciences librarians and colleagues across the Libraries, the successful candidate will support research, teaching, and learning while contributing to the university's mission of research excellence and student success. Support Social Science Research Provide specialized research assistance and consultations involving social science research, government publications and data, legislative and regulatory materials, policy documents, and international information resources. Develop and assess social science collections in collaboration with other librarians to support research and teaching needs. Lead FSU Libraries' government documents program, overseeing federal depository and other government information collections, program compliance, and specialist staff. Advance Student Learning Design and deliver instructional sessions, workshops, and course-integrated instruction, including information literacy and AI literacy, in collaboration with fellow Social Science librarians. Develop and maintain instructional materials, research guides, tutorials, and other resources that support student learning and faculty research. Build Campus Partnerships Serve as the library liaison for Political Science, Public Administration & Policy, and International Affairs, including affiliated research centers and institutes. Develop and maintain relationships with faculty, students, and campus partners to promote library resources and services and support research and instructional needs. Contribute to Professional Excellence Engage in professional development, scholarship, and/or research appropriate to faculty rank and appointment. Participate in library and university committees, professional organizations, and service activities that support the Libraries' and university's missions. Perform other duties as assigned. Qualifications Master's degree from an ALA-accredited library and information science program; or master's degree in political science, public administration, international affairs, or a closely related social science field with relevant experience in academic libraries, research support, or government information services. Knowledge of the research practices, literature, and information sources in these disciplines, including government publications and data sources. Strong communication and interpersonal skills, with the ability to provide research assistance, deliver instruction, and build collaborative relationships. Ability to coordinate projects, manage competing priorities, and work collaboratively with colleagues. Preferred Qualifications Three or more years of professional experience in an academic or research library, research support, or government information services, including providing research assistance, instruction, or liaison services. Experience with collection development or the management of specialized information resources. Experience using social science research databases, government data sources, or international statistical resources. Familiarity with the Federal Depository Library Program, government information classification systems, or government documents collection management. Knowledge of emerging trends and technologies relevant to academic librarianship, including information literacy, AI literacy, and scholarly communication. Demonstrated professional engagement through scholarship, presentations, professional organizations, or other contributions to the field. Experience supervising staff, coordinating workflows, or providing training and guidance to others. Helpful This position brings together social science librarianship and government information expertise, offering a varied portfolio of consultation, instruction, collection development, and program oversight. You will join a team of Social and Behavioral Sciences librarians while working with academic programs spanning public policy, political science, and international affairs. The role offers opportunities to apply your expertise across disciplines and support access to information for both the university and the broader community. Located within the Research & Learning Services division, this position offers an exciting opportunity to partner with faculty, graduate students, and undergraduates in the Askew School of Public Administration and Policy, the Department of Political Science, and the International Affairs Program (including Asian Studies, Latin American & Caribbean Studies, and Russian & East European Studies), along with their affiliated research centers and institutes within the College of Social Sciences and Public Policy. The position manages government information resources and expands access for the university and broader community. Contact Info Kyung Kim , Program Director for Social Sciences University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Starting at $60,000, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63350&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Elevator Shop Manager",
      "description": "Elevator Shop Manager Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63350 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities and Grounds Responsibilities Serves as a subject matter expert for vertical and horizontal transportation systems. Oversees compliance with Chapter 399, Florida Statutes, and Rule 61C-5, Florida Administrative Code. Serves as primary liaison with the Department of Business and Professional. Regulation (DBPR), Bureau of Elevator Safety. Provides direct supervision, leadership, and accountability for all Elevator Program support staff, including assigned coordinators, inspectors, and technical support personnel, ensuring effective day-to-day operations of the university elevator program. Manages campus-wide elevator maintenance control program including preventative maintenance, service interruptions, shutdowns, and return-to-service approvals. Responds to elevator entrapments and safety incidents, including after-hours emergencies. Maintains asset inventories, budgets, metrics, preventative maintenance records, and prepares reports for Facilities leadership. Coordinates inspections, permits, certificates of operation, corrective actions, and accident reporting. Oversees contracted elevator vendors, inspections, and documentation. Monitors performance, response times, safety practices, and contract compliance. Assists with procurement, renewals, invoicing, and amendments. Evaluate all FSU Facilities elevators to ensure equipment is being maintained to manufacture's specifications. Ensures safe and reliable elevator operation. Participates in elevator capital improvement planning. Coordinate with elevator vendor to evaluate campus conditions of equipment to identify if a modernization is required. Collaborate with Facilities PD&C to provide guidance and support when needed as the subject matter expert for elevator modernization. Contributes to the development of Capital Projects and Deferred Maintenance lists. Works closely with Facilities department reps, maintenance supervisors, and campus FLO personnel. Completes required safety training and complies with all safety standards including but not limited to lock out-tag out, confined space safety, safe handling of hazardous chemicals, participation in campus safety teams, and wearing required personal protective equipment (PPE). Reports complex and/or unusual problems to the Facilities Superintendent and coordinates with other Maintenance Supervisors and staff as required to complete complex tasks. Completes other relevant duties as assigned, operates university vehicles. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years experience related to facilities and/or grounds services or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63077&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Overnight Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS)",
      "description": "Overnight Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63077 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University. Responsibilities Overnight Museum Attendants patrol The Ringling's 66-acre campus on foot and with golf carts. This role is responsible for: Conducting nightly inspections of assigned areas Assisting with urgent/emergency situations in a calm and timely manner. Protecting the collection, buildings, and grounds including guarding against theft, vandalism, other damage, and the safety of those on the property. Utilizing computers to write reports, check emails, send correspondences, and submit work orders as needed. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid Florida driver’s license or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Ability to: Stand and walk for long periods Ascend/descend stairs Work in all types of weather conditions Preferred Qualifications Experience: Working in security Providing customer service Working in a museum or non-profit setting Ability to: Ability to promote a welcoming environment Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $16.48 per hour (28 hours a week) How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to wear the standard-issue uniform while at work. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours Applicants must be available for the working hours as listed below. 10:15 PM to 6:45 AM Weekends, days, or holidays may be required based on the needs of The Ringling Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63734&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - TMH Cardiology Fellowship, College of Medicine",
      "description": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - TMH Cardiology Fellowship, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63734 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University (FSU) College of Medicine , in partnership with Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH), invites applications and nominations for the position of Program Director for the Founding Program Director for the Cardiovascular Disease Fellowship Program. Responsibilities ACGME Compliance & Program Administration Accreditation Leadership: Maintain full compliance with all ACGME Common Program Requirements and Specialty-Specific Requirements for Cardiovascular Disease. Institutional Collaboration: Partner closely with the FSU College of Medicine Graduate Medical Education (GME) leadership, the Designated Institutional Official (DIO), and the Program Director of the FSU-TMH Internal Medicine Residency to ensure seamless program integration. Curriculum Design: Oversee the development, implementation, and ongoing refinement of a comprehensive 36-month cardiology curriculum that ensures COCATS Level 2 training eligibility. Recruitment: Design and lead a mission-driven, holistic recruitment and selection process for incoming fellows via ERAS and the NRMP Match. Fellow Evaluation: Direct the Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) and Program Evaluation Committee (PEC); provide timely, constructive feedback and monitor fellow milestones. Teaching & Mentorship Academic Environment: Cultivate a culture of inquiry, psychological safety, and clinical excellence. Didactics & Conferences: Oversee core educational activities, including weekly grand rounds, journal clubs, board review sessions, and regular morbidity and mortality (M&M) conferences. Scholarly Activity: Mentor fellows in research, quality improvement (QI) initiatives, and clinical case presentations, ensuring compliance with ACGME requirements for scholarship. Clinical Practice & Hospital Leadership Clinical Presence: Maintain active clinical duties at TMH in general or subspecialty cardiology (inpatient attending, consult services, and outpatient clinics). Procedural Supervision: Provide direct supervision and hands-on teaching to fellows in TMH’s advanced cardiac units, that may include the cardiac intensive care unit, echo, nuclear, catheterization, and electrophysiology labs, based on the candidate's specialty area. Qualifications Candidates must meet the strict program director criteria outlined by the ACGME: Degree: MD or DO from an accredited institution. Licensure: Eligible for an unrestricted Florida Medical License. Eligible for medical staff privileges at Tallahassee Memorial Healthcare (must be able to meet all credentialing requirements for appointment at TMH). Board Certification: Current board certification in Cardiovascular Disease by the American Board of Internal Medicine (ABIM) or the American Osteopathic Board of Internal Medicine (AOBIM). Experience: Minimum of three (3) years of documented educational and/or administrative experience as an active faculty member in an ACGME-accredited internal medicine residency or cardiovascular disease fellowship program. Scholarship: Evidence of ongoing, recent scholarly activity, including peer-reviewed publications, national presentations, or leadership roles in professional societies (e.g., ACC, AHA). Other Information FSU Health: The Evolution of Academic Healthcare FSU Health represents a bold, multi-billion-dollar transformation in healthcare delivery, clinical training, and biomedical research across North Florida. Anchored by a ultimate goal of a $1.7 billion partnership with Tallahassee Memorial Healthcare (TMH), FSU Health is transitioning the region’s premier medical assets into a fully integrated, world-class academic health center. This expanding ecosystem actively bridges bench-to-bedside research with community-focused clinical care. Key components include: The FSU Health Research Center: A state-of-the-art, 140,000-square-foot facility opening on the TMH campus to serve as a hub for clinical trials, health equity studies, and translational science. Regional Network Expansion: Rapid development of advanced clinical hubs across the Florida Panhandle, including the development of a new 100-bed hospital campus in Panama City Beach operated by TMH. Precision & Specialized Medicine: Innovations like the new FSU Health Precision Pediatrics clinic and the Florida Institute for Pediatric Rare Diseases, which bring advanced diagnostics directly to the community. The Florida State University College of Medicine Established as the first U.S. medical school of the 21st century, the FSU College of Medicine has earned national recognition for its innovative, community-based educational model. Rather than isolating training within a single university hospital, FSU utilizes a highly successful distributed model, partnering with top-tier regional healthcare systems, community clinics, and over 3,000 physician faculty members across the state. Mission-Driven Excellence: The College’s core mission focuses on developing exemplary, patient-centered physicians who are deeply responsive to community needs, with a proud legacy of excellence in training for primary care, elder care, and underserved populations. Robust GME Infrastructure: The FSU Graduate Medical Education (GME) footprint sponsors a rapidly expanding portfolio of ACGME-accredited residency and fellowship programs. GME programs under FSU sponsorship consistently achieve exceptional Match rates and board passage scores, backed by rigorous institutional oversight, a culture of psychological safety, and extensive administrative support. A Culture of Collaboration: Clinicians and program leaders at FSU enjoy access to robust academic resources, including medical informatics, instructional design experts, professional development pathways, and comprehensive research support through dedicated pre- and post-award grant infrastructure. Tallahassee Memorial HealthCare (TMH): A private, not-for-profit, 772-bed healthcare system serving a 17-county region in North Florida and South Georgia. TMH provides highly sophisticated tertiary and quaternary cardiovascular services, including structural heart interventions, advanced electrophysiology, and open-heart surgery. Southern Medical Group, P.A. (SMG) , a multi-specialty physician group providing services through a Professional Services Agreement (PSA) and Co-Management Agreement, has partnered with TMH to establish the Heart & Vascular Institute (HVI) . The HVI operates under a well-defined governance structure and strategic plan that aligns clinical, operational, and physician leadership to advance cardiovascular care across the region. Collectively, the HVI is home to one of the most advanced and highest-volume heart programs in the Southeast. Serving as a true regional epicenter for cardiovascular innovation, the HVI delivers an integrated, patient-centered cardiovascular program focused on expanding access, advancing quality, driving innovation, and improving outcomes throughout North Florida and South Georgia. The Heart & Vascular Institute features: Advanced Infrastructure: State-of-the-art hybrid cardiac/vascular suites, a dedicated biplane neurovascular suite, and a high-volume cardiac catheterization laboratory. Comprehensive Structural Heart & Electrophysiology: A highly robust structural heart program executing complex, minimally invasive interventions including TAVR, MitraClip, and Watchman implants, alongside cutting-edge heart failure neuromodulation therapies (e.g., Barostim). Top-Tier Accreditations: Recognized by the American College of Cardiology (ACC) as an Accredited Chest Pain Center with Primary PCI and Resuscitation—the highest designation available—with additional ACC certifications in Cardiac Catheterization and Transcatheter Valve procedures. National Recognition: 2026 Modern Healthcare top 50 Cardiovascular hospitals. Consistently ranked as a High-Performing Hospital by U.S. News & World Report in Heart Failure, Transcatheter Aortic Valve Replacement (TAVR), and Pacemaker Implantation. Helpful This is an exceptional leadership opportunity for a visionary cardiologist to build, shape, and direct a new ACGME-accredited 3-year General Cardiology Fellowship program. The position bridges clinical practice at TMH (a 772-bed regional medical center) with the robust educational resources and academic oversight of the FSU College of Medicine. Contact Info Heather Venclauskas Assistant Director of GME University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Negotiable based on qualifications and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm The role balance typically consists of 25% dedicated administrative/educational time and 75% clinical practice within TMH and Southern Medical Group. This is a clinical non-tenure earning position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63746&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Academic Advisor (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "Academic Advisor (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63746 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Chapman Center for Student Success and Advising Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities, and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the Emerald Coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Responsible for advising undergraduate students in the development of academic schedules appropriate for stated educational goals; takes a proactive approach in collaborating with faculty and staff for student advising purposes and provides advising services on request; interprets and recommends policies and procedures to the Director that will effectively deliver academic advisement to undergraduate students within established guidelines. Works closely with mapping coordinators within all university academic units represented on the FSU Panama City Campus in the evaluation of major-specific requirements for current and prospective students; takes a proactive approach in ensuring retention of students, student success, and timely completion of the degree. Works closely with FSU Panama City Admissions Officers to support and advise prospective transfer and first-year students. Collaborates with campus and university Admissions staff to coordinate academic advising events. Assists both on-campus and distance learning students in the enrollment and registration process; conducts follow-up with students to ensure proper course registration for timely completion of degree requirements. Assists the campus in the collection and reporting of data on all advising, retention, and student success initiatives on the Panama City campus, and any other duties assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and two years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and six years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to six years.) Preferred Qualifications Ability to effectively communicate and demonstrate advanced interpersonal skills with students and coworkers. Experience successfully contributing to a team dynamic. Expertise in using Microsoft Office, OneDrive, Microsoft Teams, and Adobe PDF programs. Ability to compile and understand student academic data. Experience with computer-based student success/enrollment management platforms (e.g., EAB Campus Connect, PeopleSoft Student Central). Contact Info Dr. Tyler Towne University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position will begin in Fall 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63716&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of MFA Lighting Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre",
      "description": "Director of MFA Lighting Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63716 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Theatre Responsibilities Florida State University’s School of Theatre invites applications for a 9 month tenure track faculty position in Lighting Design. We seek a dynamic and visionary artist-scholar to advance our graduate lighting design program, mentor students, and engage in creative and research activities that elevate the School of Theatre's profile. Teaching: Develop and teach courses in lighting design, covering introductory and advanced topics, production design, and related subjects. Participate in curriculum development and help integrate design technologies and digital media. Creative/Research Activity: Maintain an active schedule of creative work and/or research in lighting design. This may include professional design projects in theater, opera, film, television, or related fields; publications; conference presentations; and other scholarly outputs. Service: Engage in school, college, and university activities, including committee work, student advising, recruitment, and outreach. Actively support the School of Theatre’s production season by serving as a lighting designer and mentor to graduate student designers. Collaboration: Collaborate with faculty and staff from both the school and the university on interdisciplinary projects and initiatives. Connect with industry professionals and maintain ties with the broader lighting design community. Qualifications MFA in Lighting Design or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level. A strong portfolio of professional lighting design work at a national level. Evidence of ongoing creative or scholarly activity. Experience with digital design technologies, including the use of computer-aided design to create lighting design paperwork, and 3D modeling A record of successful collaboration in academic or professional settings. Contact Info Search committee chair: Jesse Dreikosen , Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates should submit the following materials: A cover letter that outlines qualifications and experience. Curriculum Vitae. A digital portfolio showcasing recent work. A teaching philosophy statement. Three letters of recommendation. Please submit all application materials through the university’s online application system. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1) After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2) Click the My References link; 3) Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4) Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to Megan Mellino , Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Applicant Review will begin November 30, 2026, and continue until filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63738&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering- Multiple Openings)",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor, 9 Month Salaried (The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering- Multiple Openings) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63738 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Department of Materials Science and Engineering in the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering invites applications from highly qualified individuals for multiple faculty positions at all ranks in the city of Tallahassee, Florida. The department sits within the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Responsibilities Establish and maintain a robust, externally funded research program with international impact and a demonstrated track record of productive, high-quality research. Foster cross-campus, interdisciplinary collaborations to enhance university research initiatives. Deliver high-quality instruction primarily at the graduate level while maintaining a strong commitment to teaching excellence. Conduct targeted outreach to undergraduate students within FAMU and FSU science and engineering departments to foster interest and engagement in the discipline. Qualifications Candidates must possess an earned Ph.D. in Materials Science, Physics, Chemistry, Engineering or a closely related discipline. Successful candidates must have a demonstrated track record of productive high-quality research. Contact Info Any questions about the positions should be directed to Search Committee Co-Chairs, Dr. Tarik Dickens dickens@eng.famu.fsu.edu or Dr. Theo Siegrist siegrist@eng.famu.fsu.edu. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Please apply to each university with the following documents: A cover letter A full curriculum vitae A 3-page research statement A 1-page teaching statement An Equal Employment Opportunity Survey for Faculty Applicants Names and contact information of three professional references. To be considered for an appointment at the rank of Assistant Professor, three letters of recommendation must be submitted directly by the letter writers at the time of application. Documents should be named 'Candidate Last Name, First Name_MS&E' and must be on letterhead with the letter writers signature included.” Faculty Information The FAMU-FSU College of Engineering is located in Innovation Park adjacent to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory (NHMFL) which houses the world’s highest field magnets and attracts well over 1000 world-wide users each year. The joint college is the nexus of two major public universities, each with a distinct mission but focused on world-class engineering education and research. Created by the Florida Legislature in 1982, the joint organization is the College of Engineering for both Florida A&M and Florida State Universities. Florida A&M is an 1890 Land Grant Institution. This unique partnership has created a truly innovative campus that leverages the benefits of the traditional HBCU with the innovations of an R-1 public research university. After completing pre-requisites at their home university, FAMU and FSU students learn, study and research together at the College campus with joint-appointed faculty and staff. Students graduate from their enrolling university AND from the FAMU-FSU College of Engineering. Both FAMU and FSU are part of the State University System of Florida. Additionally, all seven of the college’s eligible undergraduate degree programs are accredited by the Engineering Accreditation Commission of ABET Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Full consideration will be given to applications received by December 1, 2026. Applications received after that date may be considered until positions are filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63726&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - Obstetrics and Gynecology Residency Program - Sarasota Memorial Health Care System, College of Medicine",
      "description": "Program Director & Open Rank Professor, 12 Month Salaried - Obstetrics and Gynecology Residency Program - Sarasota Memorial Health Care System, College of Medicine Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63726 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Florida State University College of Medicine , in partnership with Sarasota Memorial Health Care System, seeks a visionary and accomplished academic leader to serve as the Founding Program Director (PD) for the Obstetrics and Gynecology Residency Program. Responsibilities The Program Director holds authority, accountability, and operational responsibility for all aspects of the residency program, including the integration of clinical education, resident well-being, faculty development, and strict adherence to the Accreditation Council for Graduate Medical Education (ACGME) Institutional and Program Requirements. This position balances dedicated administrative and educational leadership with ongoing clinical practice within the high-volume, high-acuity environment of Sarasota Memorial Hospital Care System. Key Responsibilities & ACGME Core Mandates 1. Program Administration & Compliance Maintain oversight and ultimate accountability for the operation of the residency program across all clinical environments. Administer and maintain an educational environment conducive to teaching and training residents in each of the six ACGME core competency areas. Ensure accurate, complete, and timely updates of all required program information in the ACGME Accreditation Data System (ADS). Implement and enforce institutional and program-specific policies regarding resident selection, evaluation, promotion, discipline, grievance, and due process. 2. Curriculum & Clinical Oversight Design, implement, and continuously improve a robust educational curriculum that reflects current trends and standards in OB/GYN education, including advanced surgical and simulation modalities. Approve the selection, continued participation, and evaluation of all core and subspecialty program faculty at participating clinical sites. Identify and collaborate with qualified Subspecialty Faculty Educators across the mandatory domains: Maternal-Fetal Medicine (MFM), Gynecologic Oncology, Female Pelvic Medicine and Reconstructive Surgery (FPMRS), and Reproductive Endocrinology and Infertility (REI). Ensure rigorous monitoring of resident supervision, appropriate clinical and educational work hours (including moonlighting policies), and safe transitions of care. 3. Resident Evaluation & Tracking Oversee the Clinical Competency Committee (CCC) to ensure objective, milestone-based evaluations of resident progression. Maintain meticulous tracking of resident operative and clinical volumes via the ACGME Case Log System, ensuring each resident comfortably achieves required procedural minimums. Provide verified, documented evidence of completion and competency for all graduating residents or those transferring laterally out of the program. 4. Academic Environment & Quality Improvement Lead the Program Evaluation Committee (PEC) in conducting the Annual Program Evaluation (APE) to assess curriculum, faculty performance, and program efficacy. Foster a robust environment of scientific inquiry, mentoring residents in quality improvement (QI) projects, patient safety initiatives, and peer-reviewed research or scholarly activities. Qualifications Education: Medical Degree (MD or DO) from an accredited institution. Certification: Current, active board certification in Obstetrics and Gynecology by the American Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (ABOG) or the American Osteopathic Board of Obstetrics and Gynecology (AOBOG). Licensure: Eligible for or currently holding an unrestricted medical license in the State of Florida. Eligible for appropriate medical staff appointments at Sarasota Memorial Healthcare (must be able to meet all credentialing requirements). Clinical Experience: A minimum of five (5) years of clinical experience in obstetrics and gynecology following completion of an OB/GYN residency. GME Experience: Minimum of three (3) years of documented educational and/or administrative experience as an active faculty member in an ACGME-accredited obstetrics and gynecology residency program. Aptitude: Demonstrated expertise in medical education pedagogy, familiarity with modern GME residency management platforms (e.g., New Innovations, Thalamus, ERAS), and an adaptive leadership approach to managing high-performing teams in high-stress clinical environments. Preferred Qualifications Leadership Track Record: Documented educational and/or administrative experience in an ACGME-accredited residency program (e.g., as an Associate Program Director, Core Faculty member, or Clerkship Director) is highly preferred. Other Information Established as the first U.S. medical school of the 21st century, the FSU College of Medicine has earned national recognition for its innovative, community-based educational model. Rather than isolating training within a single university hospital, FSU utilizes a highly successful distributed model, partnering with top-tier regional healthcare systems, community clinics, and over 3,000 physician faculty members across the state. Mission-Driven Excellence: The College’s core mission focuses on developing exemplary, patient-centered physicians who are deeply responsive to community needs, with a proud legacy of excellence in training for primary care, elder care, and underserved populations. Robust GME Infrastructure: The FSU Graduate Medical Education (GME) footprint sponsors a rapidly expanding portfolio of ACGME-accredited residency and fellowship programs. GME programs under FSU sponsorship consistently achieve exceptional Match rates and board passage scores, backed by rigorous institutional oversight, a culture of psychological safety, and extensive administrative support. A Culture of Collaboration: Clinicians and program leaders at FSU enjoy access to robust academic resources, including medical informatics, instructional design experts, professional development pathways, and comprehensive research support through dedicated pre- and post-award grant infrastructure. About Sarasota Memorial Health Care System Founded in 1925, Sarasota Memorial Health Care System (SMHCS) is a highly decorated full-service public health system, a regional medical center and the largest employer in Sarasota County. Anchored by its flagship 897-bed acute-care campus in Sarasota, Florida, the health system spans a comprehensive network of care that includes a second full-service hospital in Venice, the newly opened Milman-Kover Cancer Outpatient Pavilion (part of the Brian D. Jellison Cancer Institute), freestanding emergency rooms, and a dedicated behavioral health hospital. Across its expansive network, SMH supports approximately 11,000 employees, 2,500 medical staff members, and manages more than 2 million patient visits annually. For an incoming OB/GYN Residency Program Director, SMH offers an exceptionally robust clinical training ground. The health system manages nearly 5,000 births per year, supported by a state-of-the-art Level III Neonatal Intensive Care Unit (NICU), comprehensive maternal-fetal medicine oversight, and specialized subspecialty clinics. National Recognitions & Quality Benchmarks Sarasota Memorial is internationally recognized for its uncompromising commitment to patient safety, clinical outcomes, and nursing excellence: The CMS \"Gold Standard\": SMH is the only hospital in the state of Florida—and one of fewer than a dozen nationwide—to earn the prestigious 5-Star Quality Rating from the U.S. Centers for Medicare & Medicaid Services (CMS) every single year since the federal rating program's inception in 2016. Top 15 Health System: Named one of the nation's 15 Top Health Systems by Modern Healthcare and Premier Inc., placing it in the highest tier of high-performing U.S. healthcare delivery organizations. Magnet® Recognition: Holds over 20 consecutive years of Magnet Designation for Nursing Excellence from the American Nurses Credentialing Center, a distinction shared by less than 2% of hospitals nationwide. Safety & Specialty Accolades: Consistently achieves \"Straight A\" safety ratings from The Leapfrog Group and is repeatedly named among America's Best Hospitals by U.S. News & World Report, Newsweek, and Forbes. Designated as a Baby-Friendly Hospital in 2017 and successfully re-designated in 2023. SMH-Sarasota was the first, and remains the only hospital in southwest Florida to earn the designation from Baby-Friendly USA Inc. The organization is part of a global initiative by World Health Organization and United Nations Children's Fund to promote mother-baby bonding, successful breastfeeding and best practices in maternity care. Level III Maternal Care Verification from the Joint Commission, in collaboration with the American College of Obstetrics in 2023. Sarasota Memorial received the Level III verification for providing advanced care to low and moderate-risk pregnancies, as well as to high-risk patients, including subspecialty care for more complex maternal medical conditions, obstetric complications and fetal conditions. As an elite clinical partner to the Florida State University College of Medicine, Sarasota Memorial Health Care System provides residents and faculty with the resource-rich, high-volume environment of a premier regional powerhouse, coupled with the deeply mission-driven culture of a true community asset. Contact Info R. Bubba Hamilton Director of GME University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Negotiable, based on qualifications and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Schedule: Monday - Friday, 8:00 am - 5:00 pm Required Protected Time & Support: Administrative Allocation: In strict compliance with ACGME requirements, the Sponsoring Institution guarantees no less than 20 hours per week (0.50 FTE) of protected, non-clinical professional effort dedicated entirely to the administrative, educational, and academic activities of the Obstetrics and Gynecology program. This is a clinical non-tenure earning position. This position is being advertised as open until filled. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63551&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Senior Academic Innovation Learning Specialist",
      "description": "Senior Academic Innovation Learning Specialist Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63551 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Institute for Child Welfare Responsibilities The Senior Academic Innovation Learning Specialist coordinates and facilitates simulation-based learning, faculty development, and experiential learning initiatives that prepare students and faculty to engage effectively with Florida’s child welfare system. Key responsibilities include: Planning and coordinating simulation experiences in the Experiential Learning Lab and at university locations throughout Florida, including scheduling, logistics, university partner coordination, actor recruitment and preparation, resource management, and participant evaluation. Facilitating simulations, structured debriefs, faculty development workshops, simulation training, communities of practice, and faculty workgroups focused on experiential learning and child welfare education. Collaborating with Institute programs to pilot and implement innovative educational tools, simulations, coaching resources, and faculty and student initiatives, while serving as a backup facilitator for Institute learning events as needed. Providing child welfare subject matter expertise to support curriculum implementation, faculty consultation, simulation development, conference presentations, webinars, and educational outreach. Strengthening relationships with universities and faculty across Florida and expanding the Institute’s capacity to deliver consistent, high-quality experiential learning opportunities statewide. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and four years' experience related to health and human services or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) Preferred Qualifications Master’s degree in social work, education, instructional design, child and family studies, public administration, or a related field. Direct experience working in Florida’s child welfare system or supporting Florida’s child welfare workforce. Experience facilitating simulation-based learning, experiential learning, role-play activities, or case-based instruction. Experience designing or implementing simulations, including scenario preparation, actor coordination, facilitation, and participant debriefing. Experience working with institutions of higher education, university faculty, or students. Experience facilitating faculty development workshops, communities of practice, or collaborative workgroups. Experience providing child welfare subject matter expertise for curriculum development or implementation. Experience piloting or implementing innovative learning tools, educational technologies, or interdisciplinary learning initiatives. Experience delivering presentations, webinars, or conference sessions to professional audiences. Knowledge of evaluation methods used to assess participant learning and program outcomes. Helpful The Florida Institute for Child Welfare is housed at the Florida State University College of Social Work. The purpose of the institute is to advance the well-being of children and families by improving the performance of child protection and child welfare services through research, policy analysis, evaluation, and leadership development. Suggested to visit The Florida Institute for Child Welfare for more information. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Anticipated salary between low to mid $60,000's, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicant need not apply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63073&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "1st Shift Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS)",
      "description": "1st Shift Museum Attendants (Part-Time/OPS) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63073 Location Sarasota, FL Full/Part Time Part-Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The John & Mable Ringling Museum of Art is located in Sarasota, Florida, and is a department of Florida State University . Responsibilities Primary responsibilities include: Patrols The Ringling's 66 acres of buildings, galleries, and grounds as assigned. Monitor visitor activity to ensure: Safety of staff and visitors Adherence to all policies/procedures Protection of the collection, buildings, and grounds while guarding against theft, vandalism, and other damage Briefly answers guest questions with a focus on customer service and creating a welcoming environment for our visitor population. Conducts daily inspections of assigned areas and reports: Safety issues Damages or necessary repairs Water intrusion or leaks As needed: Assists with emergency situations by communicating with the appropriate point of contact. Escorting staff and guests as assigned. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalent Valid Florida driver's license or the ability to obtain one prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Experience with: Customer service and creating a welcoming environment Museums or similar non-profit organizations Ability to: Respond calmly to urgent/emergency situations Effectively communicate with the public Pay attention to surroundings and report issues Contact Info For more information or technical assistance, please contact Ringling Human Resources via email or by calling 941-358-2771. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $15.45 (28 hours a week) This role is eligible for a $5 per hour pay additive for working eligible assigned special events. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . Work Location: Sarasota, FL Employees are required to wear the standard-issue uniform while at work. This position is being readvertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Working Hours This role has a set bi-weekly schedule. Applicants must be available for the schedule as listed below. Week 1: Saturday, Sunday, Tuesday, and Wednesday from 9:30 AM to 5:00 PM. Week 2: Friday and Monday from 9:30 AM to 5:00 PM, and Thursday from 9:30 AM to 8:00 PM. Weekends, evenings, and holidays may be required per the needs of the Ringling. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63715&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Deputy Building Official",
      "description": "Deputy Building Official Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63715 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department FSU Facilities Environmental Health and Safety Department Responsibilities Conduct review of construction documents and construction inspections of University Building Projects for Compliance with Florida Building Code. Act as assistant to the University's Building Official in the accomplishment of the mission of the Building Code Administration section to ensure that construction and maintenance activities on University facilities comply with the appropriate regulations. Perform supervisory activities of BCA sections staff to include coordination of daily work efforts, educational opportunities and requirements. Interact with all construction project team members (University Project Manager, Design Professionals and Contractor and Sub-Contractor personnel) to ensure compliance with Florida Building Code is maintained. Assist in the development and implementation of policies and procedures associated with the activities of the Building & Fire Safety sections. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: or a combination of post high school education and experience equal to seven years) Possess or obtain within 120 days of employment standard or provisional FL license as plans reviewer & inspector in two disciplines (Building, Mechanical, Plumbing, Electrical, Fire) in accordance with FS 468. Possess or obtain within one year of employment FL Building Code Administrative license. A valid Florida or Georgia driver's license or the ability to obtain one upon hire. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63713&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of MFA Costume Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre",
      "description": "Director of MFA Costume Design / Open Rank Faculty, 9 Month Salaried - School of Theatre Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63713 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department School of Theatre Responsibilities The School of Theatre at Florida State University seeks a full-time nine-month, tenure-track open rank faculty position in Costume Design. We seek a dynamic and visionary artist-scholar to advance our graduate costume design program, mentor students, and engage in creative and research activities that elevate the School of Theatre's profile. Teaching : Responsibilities include teaching three courses per semester, which may include costume design, costume rendering, and costume history. Creative/Research Activity: Maintain an active schedule of creative work and/or research in costume design. Service : This position requires active*departmental participation, including curriculum development, recruitment, student advising, and season planning. Collaboration : Collaborate with faculty and staff from both the school and the university on interdisciplinary projects and initiatives. Connect with industry professionals and maintain ties with the broader costume design community. Communication : The applicant must be able to communicate effectively with costume graduate and undergraduate students and collaborate successfully with directors, faculty, and staff. Qualifications MFA in Costume Design or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Advanced expertise in rendering, costume design, and computer rendering Knowledge of historical period costume Experience in millinery construction, fabric modification, and costume crafts Demonstrated excellence in teaching at the university level. A strong portfolio of professional costume design work at a national level. Evidence of ongoing creative or scholarly activity. A record of successful collaboration in academic or professional settings. Contact Info Search committee chair: Jacki Armit , Associate Professor University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates should submit the following materials: A cover letter that outlines qualifications and experience. Curriculum Vitae. A digital portfolio or website showcasing recent work. A teaching philosophy statement. Three letters of recommendation. Please submit all application materials through the university’s online application system. Incomplete applications will not be considered. Confidential Letters of Reference: This position requires that you have three confidential professional letters of recommendation submitted on your behalf. Follow the steps below to request these letters through our system: 1. After submitting your application, click the Explore Jobs link; 2. Click the My References link; 3. Click the Send/View Reference Request button next to the appropriate position; and 4. Follow the steps on that page to send your references a system generated email requesting they submit a letter of recommendation on your behalf. You may also return to the My References link and click on \"Send/View Reference Request\" to see if your references have responded, add additional references, or resend requests. Candidates who currently hold tenure and are seeking appointment with tenure at Florida State University will need to submit the materials for evaluation if selected. These materials are required to support the tenure review process at the time of hire. Finalists may be asked to provide the below additional documentation as part of the evaluation. Examples of excellence in research or creative activity or excellence in teaching. CV One-page statement of their accomplishments over the last five years. Discussion of their teaching, research and service (no longer than six pages). Three outside letters of recommendation directed specifically to Florida State University. No professional relationships should exist between the candidate and the external reviewer. Relationships include, but are not limited to, student- teacher (including dissertation committee chairs and members), colleagues in graduate school, former departmental colleagues, collaborators, and co-authors. These letters should be sent to Megan Mellino , Administrative Specialist, directly from the external reviewer. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . This position is being advertised as open until filled and will begin Fall 2027. Applicant Review will begin November 30, 2026, and continue until filled. The faculty rank associated with the appointment will be determined based on the selected candidate’s qualifications and experience. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63727&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Full time- Program Assistant (CIVICS Seal of Excellence Project)",
      "description": "OPS Full time- Program Assistant (CIVICS Seal of Excellence Project) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63727 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department The Learning Systems Institute Responsibilities • Data entry, filing, and record keeping • Track suppliers and payments • Manage large quantities of data in Excel • Organize and maintain office supplies and clean workspace • Other related duties as assigned by the supervisor Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency. Must be able to work in office in Tallahassee, Florida. Preferred Qualifications • Familiarity with OMNI and Payment Works. • Experience with Microsoft Office, particularly Microsoft Word, and/or Excel is strongly preferred Contact Info Marissa Love mlove@lsi.fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Rate: $20.00 per hour. This position is full-time at 40 hours per week. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position does not begin until JANUARY 2027. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63247&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Technical Research Designer, Level I (Control Room - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory)",
      "description": "Technical Research Designer, Level I (Control Room - National High Magnetic Field Laboratory) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63247 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Join the world-renowned National High Magnetic Field Laboratory at Florida State University (FSU) and support groundbreaking scientific discovery in a collaborative, high-tech environment. FSU was recently recognized as one of America’s Best-in-State Employers for its strong workplace culture and employee-centered values. Responsibilities Operate and maintain facility equipment and systems in support of the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory’s DC high magnetic field user program. Interact with and assist users, research faculty, technicians and other National High Magnetic Field Laboratory staff on the operation and maintenance of the facility. Facility Operations & System Monitoring Monitor and safely operate facility equipment and systems. Coordinate with the City of Tallahassee’s Electrical Distribution Control Room with regards to facility operations and power levels. Take the proper corrective actions in response to alarms or other indications of abnormal equipment operation. Exercise skilled independent judgement in handling facility operations as well as unexpected or emergency situations. Distributed Control System (DCS) Engineering Perform engineering functions on the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory Distributed Control System (DCS) such as graphic, trend group and control group building, logic development and troubleshooting, field device integration. Use knowledge of the DCS to perform troubleshooting between the DCS and field devices. Safety & Compliance Coordinate, prepare and issue Lock, Tag, Verify procedures for facility maintenance, troubleshooting and repair in accordance with National High Magnetic Field Laboratory safety policies and procedures. Work with other National High Magnetic Field Laboratory personnel in the evaluation and development of safety policies and procedures. Take a proactive attitude and make solution-oriented contributions to the National High Magnetic Field Laboratory safety program. Maintenance & System Performance Assist Facility engineers, staff and scientists with the development of preventative maintenance programs and procedures. Assist Facility engineers and staff in tracking the performance and characteristics of the water-cooled magnets. Contribute to equipment and system characterization, troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance, installation, integration and commissioning. Training & User Support Provide training to users and staff on safe magnet operations, safe overhead crane operations and other safety procedures as necessary. Engineering Support & Projects In consultation with supervisor(s) and design engineers, assist with determining changes in design and operation of plant and power equipment to improve operations, capabilities, reliability and uptime. Contribute to facility projects. Giving tours. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent and four years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Helpful What You Gain at FSU Opportunity to work at a world-renowned national research laboratory. Meaningful contributions to scientific discovery and student learning. A collaborative environment that values your expertise and invests in your growth. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range Minimum salary of $47,660, commensurate with education and experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Participate in on-call duties. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63731&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Analytics Architect",
      "description": "Analytics Architect Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63731 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department This position is within FSU’s Department of Information Technology Services (ITS) The Data & Analytics team at Florida State University connects, manages, and delivers data that powers decision-making across campus. We build the pipelines, reporting, predictive models and analytics that help leaders understand student success, operations, and institutional performance, and we’re advancing AI-enabled tools to make that insight easier to use. Responsibilities Analytics Architects use critical thinking skills and exercise their judgment to discover the patterns and information found in vast amounts of data using analytics predictive models and machine learning. The incumbent makes sense of these patterns and signals to help the university make better decisions which will lead to better service for our students, faculty, community partners, and staff. An effective analytics architect will also be adept at providing an explanatory narrative that a non-expert can follow and understand. Responsible for supporting the University's data and analytic needs across multiple sources of data. Designs, develops, analyses, and supports the creation of information products in alignment with functional and technical system requirements. Develops programming code and scripting using appropriate language and tools to provide problem resolutions and new functionality in complex analytical systems. Responsible for reviewing and capturing business requirements needed for a new design, development, and maintenance of analytical models, and process modifications, and performing the technical development based on these requirements. Will also provide recommendations and narratives explaining the value of the models. Responsible for conducting testing scenarios to ensure the integrity of analytical products and processes and validation of all applications, Provides recommendations for enhancements to existing systems. Responsible for the creation and maintenance of system specifications and documented requirements pertaining to analytical products, models, and processes. Performs duties in compliance with ITS policies, guidelines, and processes pertaining to support requests, work orders, project management, change management, and incident management. Appropriately utilizes associated tools in accordance with ITS standards. Qualifications Bachelor's degree in Computer Science, MIS, or other appropriate degree and three years' experience or a high school diploma or equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: or an equivalent combination of education and experience.) Preferred Qualifications Prior experience with Microsoft Power BI or similar visualization tool and Snowflake. Practical experience with SQL including CTEs and ranking/partition functions. Helpful Who is an ideal candidate for this position? Someone who enjoys dealing directly with stakeholders to capture requirements and collaborating with colleagues. What is a typical day in this position? A typical day may involve building an information or data product from scratch or reengineering a legacy dashboard or logical view. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63704&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Associate Vice Provost, Academic Policy and Faculty Affairs (Open Rank Professor, 12-Month Salaried)",
      "description": "Associate Vice Provost, Academic Policy and Faculty Affairs (Open Rank Professor, 12-Month Salaried) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63704 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Faculty Development & Advancement Responsibilities The Associate Vice Provost for Academic Policy and Faculty Affairs provides university-wide leadership for academic policy administration, curriculum governance and the fair and consistent resolution of academic matters. Working across colleges and administrative units, the position oversees critical academic systems and regulatory processes; promotes institutional compliance with university, Board of Governors, and state requirements; and serves as a central liaison on curriculum, syllabi, student conduct, appeals, and academic integrity. The role also supervises designated staff and supports data-informed decision-making that advances faculty effectiveness and the university’s academic mission. Responsibilities of the Position: Provide strategic and operational oversight of Coursedog, the university’s curriculum management platform, ensuring alignment with institutional curriculum policies. Serve as the principal Faculty Development and Advancement liaison to department chairs, deans, and college curriculum leaders regarding course proposals, approval pathways, and policy implementation. Collaborate with the Office of Digital Learning to oversee the institutional implementation and administration of Simple Syllabus, including governance, adoption, and compliance with university and Board of Governors syllabus requirements. Work closely with college leadership on institutional compliance with Board of Governors Regulation 8.003, including coordination and monitoring and reporting of faculty attestations every semester. Administer and ensure university compliance with Florida’s Statewide Articulation Framework under section 1007.23, Florida Statutes, and the Common Prerequisite Manual, coordinating policy interpretation and implementation across academic units. Serve as the primary Faculty Development and Advancement liaison to the Division of Student Affairs and serve as the office’s representative on the Behavioral Intervention Team, facilitating coordinated responses to complex student matters with academic implications. Serve as the primary Faculty Development and Advancement liaison to the Student Ombuds, coordinating consultation and follow-up on academic concerns that require central administrative review. Supervise the Academic Affairs Administrator responsible for administration of the Academic Honor Policy, ensuring consistent procedures, timely case management, effective training and guidance, and compliance with university requirements. Supervise the Academic Affairs Administrator responsible for administration and fiscal operations of the Faculty Senate and Faculty Senate Steering Committee. Provide central review and guidance for general academic appeals that remain unresolved at the instructor, department, or college level, ensuring fair, timely, and policy-consistent resolution. Coordinate Faculty Development and Advancement review of grade appeals elevated to the Student Academic Relations Committee, while supporting consistent application of university policy. Evaluate academic policies and processes and propose changes to enhance effectiveness. This also includes the approval or denial of requests for exceptions to academic rules submitted to Faculty Development and Advancement for consideration. These decisions should be documented and applied consistently according to university standards. Represent Faculty Development and Advancement as an ex officio member of the University Curriculum Committee. Assist in leadership development programming related to the areas of responsibility outlined in this job description. Qualifications The successful candidate must have a doctoral degree (or terminal degree for the field). Preference will be given to faculty who are tenured and at the highest rank for their position. The successful candidate will have at least three years of experience in an administrative role in an academic unit (e.g., department, school) or at the college level. Experience in supervising staff is highly valued as is direct experience with the creation and implementation of academic policies at the unit and/or college level. The successful candidate will have the following characteristics: Highly organized and efficient in managing complex processes Excellent communications skills (written and oral) Curiosity about academic affairs processes and systems at the university level Self-starter who can perform independently but seeks advice appropriately Motivated to develop a deep understanding of academic affairs policies and procedures Appreciation for technology that is used in administering academic affairs policies and procedures Fair minded and able to listen to multiple viewpoints while also applying academic policies and guidelines consistently Ability to work effectively with multiple stakeholder offices (e.g., colleges; Division of Student Affairs; Institutional Research) Collaborative and able to work with a wide array of people in various positions (students, staff, faculty, department chairs, associate deans, deans, and senior leadership) Strong instincts for tracking down answers and identifying relevant policies to resolve academic affairs issues Strong interest in advancing the academic excellence of the university Contact Info For inquiries regarding the application and search process, please contact Craig Stanley, chair of the Search Advisory Committee. Email: cstanley@fsu.edu Phone: 850-644-6876 University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information and include education details. Applicants must submit a letter of interest in the position and curriculum vitae. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=62817&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "OPS Testing Center Support, Office of Accessibility Services - Fall 2026",
      "description": "Job Title OPS Testing Center Support, Office of Accessibility Services - Fall 2026 Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 62817 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Regular/Temporary Temporary Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of Accessibility Services | Department of Student Support & Transitions Responsibilities The responsibilities include directing visitors, answering and managing incoming calls, handling inquiries, and providing administrative support to various departments. The position will be primarily testing and transportation support. Qualifications High school diploma/equivalent. Preferred Qualifications This role requires a professional and courteous demeanor, excellent communications skills, and the ability to manage multiple tasks efficiently. Preference for graduate students. Contact Info Amber Wagner Director of the Office of Accessibility Services / Assistant Dean of Students 850-644-9566 DOS_OAS_Admin@fsu.edu University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an OPS/temporary job. Based on the duties, this position may require completion of a criminal history background check . This position's schedule is M-F, 8 AM - 5 PM. This position is being re-advertised. Previous applicants need not reapply. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63675&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) (Multiple Openings)",
      "description": "Assistant Professor, 9 Month Salaried (Finance - Herbert Wertheim College of Business) (Multiple Openings) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63675 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Department of Finance Herbert Wertheim College of Business The Department of Finance provides an active research environment including the Truist seminar series and the Truist Beach Conference. Faculty have access to summer research grants, graduate student research assistants, travel support and an excellent collection of databases. Responsibilities Florida State University's Herbert Wertheim College of Business seeks applications for a tenure-track Assistant Professor position in Finance. The incumbent is expected to teach at the undergraduate and/or graduate levels and develop a research agenda that targets top-tier journals. Candidates with expertise in Wealth Management are invited to apply. The position is scheduled to start in Fall 2027 Qualifications Candidates for this position must have earned or be near completion of a Ph.D. in Finance or Financial Economics. Degree must be conferred by August 1, 2027. Contact Info Please contact Irena Hutton if you have any questions. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Florida State University is a Carnegie-classified R1 research university located in Tallahassee, Florida, the state capital, with enrollment exceeding 46,000 students. In the 2027 U.S. News & World Report Best Colleges rankings, Florida State ranks No. 59 among national universities and No. 24 among public universities in the United States. The Herbert Wertheim College of Business enrolls approximately 8,500 students seeking business degrees across undergraduate, master’s, and doctoral programs. The Department of Finance offers programs and courses at the undergraduate, master’s, and Ph.D. levels. Graduate offerings include the Master of Science in Finance (MSF), the Ph.D. in Business Administration with a major in Finance, and MBA programs offered in full-time, evening, and online formats. Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Candidates graduating in 2026/2027 are also required to submit transcripts. Review of applications will begin immediately. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled or March 1, 2027. Please send recommendation letters to Irena Hutton . Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63640&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Director of Stamps Program, ONF, PSP - Instructional Specialist I, 12 Month Salaried",
      "description": "Director of Stamps Program, ONF, PSP - Instructional Specialist I, 12 Month Salaried Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63640 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Office of National Fellowships Presidential Scholars Program Stamps Scholars Program Undergraduate Studies Responsibilities We are seeking an experienced and innovative higher education program administrator to help us launch our partnership with the Stamps Scholars program, as well as work collaboratively with our premier, merit scholarship program, the Presidential Scholars, and with our Office of National Fellowships. Strategic Program Leadership Provides strategic leadership and administrative oversight for a portfolio of high-impact scholar and fellowship programs to include the Stamps Scholars Program, Office of National Fellowships, and Presidential Scholars Program. Serves as primary lead for the Stamps Scholars Program. Oversees program planning, operations, assessment, reporting, budget management, and implementation of initiatives that support student success and advance institutional goals. Develops and maintains strong relationships with university leadership, donors, faculty, and external partners to enhance program effectiveness and expand opportunities for students. Teaching and Student Development Teaches Presidential Scholars seminars and facilitates educational experiences that promote academic excellence, interdisciplinary learning, leadership growth, and student engagement. Responsible for curricular development including objectives, revisions, and teaching assignments. Responsible for updating Simple Syllabus and Coursedog. Guides students in exploring scholarship and fellowship opportunities, research experiences, graduate and professional school preparation, career planning, and other developmental pathways. Student Recruitment, Success, and Enrichment Leads efforts to recruit, retain, and support highly motivated students through innovative academic, leadership, service, and co-curricular programming. Designs and implements transformative student experiences that foster intellectual engagement, leadership development, research and creative activity, civic responsibility, and post-graduate success. Provides advising and mentorship to students as they pursue academic, professional, and personal development opportunities. Team Leadership and Fellowship Advancement Provides leadership and supervision for professional and student staff supporting the Presidential Scholars Program and Office of National Fellowships. Oversees fellowship advising, application support, campus nomination processes, outreach initiatives, and applicant development efforts that increase participation and success in nationally competitive scholarships and fellowships. Leads operational planning, staff development, and continuous improvement efforts while fostering collaborative partnerships across the university and beyond. Assessment and Continuous Improvement Evaluates program effectiveness using measures of student engagement, retention, academic achievement, leadership development, post-graduate outcomes, and fellowship success. Uses data to inform continuous improvement and prepares reports and recommendations for the Associate Dean and university stakeholders. Qualifications Master's degree and three years of experience in higher education program management. Preferred Qualifications Demonstration of strong interpersonal skills and the ability to effectively work with a wide range of individuals and constituencies in a community, and the ability to foster a cooperative work environment. Experience managing and overseeing an operating budget. Ability to provide subject matter expertise and counsel others. Ability to develop and implement policies, procedures, goals, and objectives. Ability to evaluate process effectiveness and develop change or alternatives. Ability to train and supervise employees. Contact Info Dr. Craig Filar University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . Anticipated Salary Range $75,000 - $80,000, commensurate with education & experience. FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific Faculty job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Faculty Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include education details even if attaching a Vita. Note: A cover letter outlining your interest and relevant experience is also required as part of your submission. Considerations This is a Faculty position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . First round of applications will be reviewed in November 2026. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63781&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Research Engineer, Level II-IV - DC Field User Facility (NHMFL)",
      "description": "Research Engineer, Level II-IV - DC Field User Facility (NHMFL) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63781 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department National High Magnetic Field Laboratory - DC Field User Facility Responsibilities Responsible for selecting and applying standard engineering techniques and procedures for the construction, repair and maintenance of highly specialized scientific research equipment in collaboration with scientists and users. Involvement from conception of idea, design and construction of new apparatus. Assist users in carrying out experiments in a variety of superconducting and resistive magnet cells. Assist with policy development for overall user program. Maintain technical knowledge and expertise of all specialized equipment in order to identify short and long range instrumentation needs. Assist with the development and direction of the user program. Analyze problems with research equipment. Arrange with vendors or NHMFL shops for repair of instruments. Keep records of equipment shipped and received Order, receive, and distribute supplies, instrumentation and tools. Assist with providing software and data acquisition support to users and other NHMFL project teams. Other duties as assigned, including participation in Open House and other outreach activities. Serve on committees that promote safety, operational efficiency, and a productive working environment. Qualifications Bachelor's degree and three years of experience; or a high school diploma/equivalent and seven years of experience. (Note: post-high school education can substitute for experience at the equivalent rate.) Candidates with an additional three years of related experience will be considered for levels Ill - VI. Each level requires an additional three years of related experience. Contact Info For additional information, please contact Kayla West . University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63767&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "School Psychologist - FSUS",
      "description": "School Psychologist - FSUS Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63767 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida State University Schools Responsibilities Conduct comprehensive assessments and evaluations for students suspected of disabilities and gifted eligibility. Analyzes and interprets assessment data; completes evaluation and re-evaluation reports; conducts Functional Behavioral Assessments (FBAs) as needed; facilitates and participates in eligibility, staffing, and gifted determination meetings; provides feedback and present evaluation findings to parents, teachers, and multidisciplinary teams; makes recommendations for services, accommodations, interventions, and educational supports; and maintains required evaluation documentation. Participates as a member of the MTSS/Problem-Solving Team. Reviews student data, assists with intervention planning, attends team meetings, and provides recommendations regarding academic and behavioral concerns. Consults with teachers, administrators, student services staff, parents, and other appropriate personnel regarding learning, behavioral, social-emotional, and academic concerns. Prepares and maintains required records, completes documentation in a timely manner, and performs additional duties as necessary related to the district’s student mental health and assessment needs. Qualifications Master's degree or higher from an accredited educational institution with state certification in School Psychology, on or before the time of hire. Other Information We proudly serve as a laboratory K-12 school, blending the rigors of academic achievement with a commitment to educational research and innovation. We draw upon the resources of a world-class university, bringing cutting-edge practices and insights directly into our classrooms. This dynamic approach ensures that our students benefit from the latest advancements in pedagogy and fosters an environment where curiosity and exploration are celebrated. Florida State University Schools is not just a place of learning; it's a community dedicated to empowering the leaders of tomorrow. We invite you to explore the possibilities at FSUS and join us on a journey of academic excellence, personal growth, and a commitment to making a positive impact on the world. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check , including a fingerprint-based screening via AHCA’s Clearinghouse pursuant to Section 1012, Florida Statutes, for positions in a FSU Developmental Research School or Section 409.175, Florida Statutes, for positions in a Childcare or Summer Camp position. Visit the AHCA Clearinghouse Screenings webpage for more information. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63769&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "General Trades Technician (Panama City Campus)",
      "description": "General Trades Technician (Panama City Campus) Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63769 Location Panama City, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department PCC Finance and Administration Department About Us | FSU Panama City Florida State University is one of the nation’s top public universities and FSU Panama City amplifies the university’s efforts to preserve, expand, and disseminate knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and human services professions. FSU Panama City is located 100 miles west of Tallahassee on the beautiful North St. Andrews Bay and is only three miles from the beaches of the emerald coast. FSU PC currently houses 20 bachelor's programs, 9 master's programs, and 1 doctoral program, and boasts a small faculty-to-student ratio, which gives students a more personalized academic experience. Please visit https://pc.fsu.edu/promise for information about our FSU PC Promise to students and https://pc.fsu.edu/ for more information about our campus. FSU Panama City also recently opened a brand new, residential housing complex on campus and right on the water. This new apartment-style complex at FSU PC houses both undergraduate and graduate students. For more information about our on-campus housing, visit https://seminolelandingfsu.com/ . Responsibilities Responsible for inspections, preventative and repair maintenance to ensure all buildings, grounds, and equipment are in safe operating condition. Reports maintenance needs to supervisor. Responsible for maintenance of groundskeeping, landscaping, irrigation system, campus roadways, and parking areas. Responsible for troubleshooting and repair of building maintenance, which consists of painting, drywall, carpentry, A/C systems, electrical systems, pumping systems including water and sewer lines, doors and windows, gas and electric welding, and soldering as needed. Generates and responds to emails and work orders via the online work order system. Updates work order system daily regarding progress and/or upon completion of assignment. Assists with set-ups for special functions on and off campus. Qualifications High school diploma or equivalency and two years of experience, or a combination of post-high school education and experience equal to two years. (A technical or vocational degree may substitute for experience.). A valid State of Florida or Georgia Driver’s License or the ability to obtain prior to hire. Preferred Qualifications Technical or vocational training in facilities maintenance, construction, HVAC, plumbing, or electrical trades. Experience working in higher education, healthcare, or large-scale public facilities. OSHA 10 or OSHA 30 General Industry Safety Certification. Proficient in the use of hand tools, power tools, and maintenance equipment safely. Strong problem-solving and troubleshooting abilities. Experience reading work orders, blueprints, or maintenance manuals. Reliable, self-motivated, and able to work independently or as part of a team. Good communication and record-keeping skills. Notes where maintenance or repairs are required and reports any problems to supervisors. Helpful During the first three months, the General Trades Technician will receive structured, hands-on training to build familiarity with campus systems, tools, and safety procedures. The selected candidate will work closely with their supervisor and department head to: Participate in guided training sessions on university equipment, facilities, and standard operating procedures. Shadow experienced staff to learn daily workflows and preventative maintenance practices. Gain an understanding of department safety protocols and compliance requirements. Take on progressively more independent assignments with ongoing support and feedback. Establish strong working relationships with team members and campus partners. By the end of the first 90 days, the technician is expected to be confident in navigating campus facilities, performing routine maintenance tasks, and contributing independently to the department's work while continuing to develop advanced skills. Contact Info Direct inquiries to David Gary for more information about this position. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Veterans' Preference Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, Certain service members and veterans, and the spouses and family members of such service members and veterans, receive preference and priority, and certain service members may be eligible to receive waivers for post secondary educational requirements, in employment by the state and its political subdivisions and are encouraged to apply for the positions being filled. Veterans' Preference applies to University Support Personnel System (USPS) positions only. IMPORTANT: To claim Veterans' Preference, select “yes” to the question on the application questionnaire and upload a DD-214 (or equivalent), the Veterans' Preference Certification form, and other documentation if applicable with your online application before midnight of the position closing date. Click the links for Veterans’ Preference eligibility requirements and Veterans’ Preference required documentation (PDF) , or call FSU Human Resources at (850) 644-6034 . Considerations This is an USPS (University Support Personnel System) position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . The position will begin in Fall 2026. Schedule will be Monday through Friday, 8:00 AM to 4:30 PM. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
    },
    "https://jobs.omni.fsu.edu/psc/sprdhr_er/EMPLOYEE/HRMS/c/HRS_HRAM_FL.HRS_CG_SEARCH_FL.GBL?Page=HRS_APP_JBPST_FL&Action=U&FOCUS=Applicant&SiteId=1&JobOpeningId=63783&PostingSeq=1": {
      "title": "Grants Administrator - Florida Center for Interactive Media",
      "description": "Grants Administrator - Florida Center for Interactive Media Next Job Apply for Job Job ID 63783 Location Tallahassee, FL Full/Part Time Full-Time Regular/Temporary Regular Add to My Favorite Jobs Email this Job Department Florida Center for Interactive Media Responsibilities Works directly with Bureau leadership and staff and other FDOE Departments to ensure timely and accurate collection and dissemination of funding information. Leads the project team activities and staff related to discretionary projects/entitlement grants administration and management. Develops and prepares timely trackers, reports and publications for dissemination and ensures their accuracy. Supports FDOE leadership through technical assistance, interpreting policies and procedures, and assisting in the implementation of goals and objectives to provide services for students with disabilities. Provides assistance to both state and district staff, fiscal agencies, and other stakeholders related to project/grant administration. Leads/participates in workgroups and helps plan meetings. Creates and delivers presentations and ensures the appropriateness and accuracy of the fiscal team's products and presentations. Performs other duties as assigned. Qualifications A Bachelor's degree and four years of experience; or a high school diploma or equivalent and eight years of experience. (Note: a combination of post high school education and experience equal to eight years.) This position requires successful completion of the eSPEAR Certification or ability to obtain the certification within 6 months of hire. https://www.research.fsu.edu/research-offices/sra/resources/training/espear/. University Information One of the nation's elite research universities, Florida State University preserves, expands, and disseminates knowledge in the sciences, technology, arts, humanities, and professions, while embracing a philosophy of learning strongly rooted in the traditions of the liberal arts and critical thinking. Founded in 1851, Florida State University is the oldest continuous site of higher education in Florida. FSU is a community steeped in tradition that fosters research and encourages creativity. At FSU, there’s the excitement of being part of a vibrant academic and professional community, surrounded by people whose ideas are shaping tomorrow’s news! Learn more about Florida State University and our campuses . FSU Total Rewards FSU offers a robust Total Rewards package. Visit our FSU Total Rewards website to learn more about our Compensation, Benefits, Wellness, Recognition, and Employee Development programs. Use our FSU Total Compensation Calculato r to calculate Total Compensation options based on potential salary, benefits and retirement contributions, earned leave, and other employment-related perks. How To Apply If qualified and interested in a specific job opening as advertised, apply through the FSU Careers site (jobs.fsu.edu). If you are a current FSU employee, apply through myFSU Self Service. Applicants are required to complete the online application with all applicable information. Applications must include all work history up to ten years, and education details even if attaching a resume. Considerations This is an A&P position. This position requires successful completion of a criminal history background check . A Level 2 background check conducted by FLDOE is required for this position. Equal Employment Opportunity FSU is an Equal Employment Opportunity Employer. Apply for Job"
